    "work_product": "identity and ownership verification brief for synthetic blue harbor logistics intake profiling evidence segment ctx001 — evidence-integrated revision",
    "full_prompt": "MATERIAL 1:\nONBOARDING ACTIVITY PROFILE\n\nObserved relationship as at 2026-04-15\n\nRECENT FLOWS FIRST\nObserved on | Payment rail | Amount | Counterparty description\n--- | --- | --- | ---\n2026-04-03 | incoming ACH | $279,500.00 | customer receipts batch\n2026-04-06 | domestic wire | $134,700.00 | equipment supplier\n2026-04-11 | international wire | $55,500.00 | overseas vendor\n\nEXPECTED PATTERN\nMonthly credits $3,826,666.67; monthly debits $3,482,266.67; domestic wires 39; international wires 6. Products requested: operating cash management, credit facility review, investment-policy reporting. Anticipated source: operating revenue and documented owner equity.\n\nWHO THE CLIENT IS\nBlue Harbor Logistics Holdings LLC was formed in Virginia on 2009-05-26 and operates in regional freight and warehousing. Tax identifier: XX-XXX0010. Principal location: 231 Commerce Way, Suite 203, Virginia.\n\nWHO CONTROLS IT\n— Marcus Vale holds 44.0% and acts as Chief Executive Officer.\n— Iris Chen holds 36.0% and acts as Chief Operating Officer.\n— Harbor Employee Trust holds 20.0% and acts as Employee trust.\n\nWHO MAY ACT\n— Marcus Vale: primary signer (verified).\n— Avery Chen: finance contact only (not verified).\n\nBALANCE-SHEET PROFILE\nCash / A/R / inventory: $2,035,000.00 / $8,420,000.00 / $640,000.00\nSenior debt: $11,700,000.00\nAnnual revenue / EBITDA: $45,920,000.00 / $4,010,000.00\n\nRISK PARAMETERS\nBusiness objective: fleet replacement and consolidation of equipment notes\nLiquidity minimum: $1,119,250.00\nRisk setting: moderate\nProhibited usage: cryptocurrency transfers, bearer instruments, undocumented third-party payments\nMonitoring note: Fuel surcharge recovery lagged diesel-cost changes by an average of 43 days in Q4 2025.\n\nSUPPORTING FILES\ncertificate of formation—present, 2009-05-26; ownership schedule—present, 2025-12-31; 2025 financial statements—present, 2025-12-31; secondary contact authority evidence—absent; current insurance certificate—absent\n\nMATERIAL 2:\nOPERATIONS BREAK CASE RECORD\n\nCase entity: Blue Harbor Logistics Holdings LLC\nPosition date: 2026-06-27\n\nOPEN CASES\nBreak reference | Finding | Amount at risk | Open since | Desk | Backup\n--- | --- | --- | --- | --- | ---\nEX-26-401 | cash break | $20,000.00 | 2026-06-26 | Cash Control | received\nEX-26-402 | missing confirmation | $560,000.00 | 2026-06-24 | Trade Support | not received\n\nRECONCILIATION NARRATIVE\nExternal cash of $2,085,000.00 exceeds recorded cash of $2,035,000.00. A $30,000.00 timing item is documented, leaving $20,000.00 unresolved.\n\nDIFFERENCE OWNERSHIP\nDEP-26-5103 → Treasury Operations | $30,000.00 | age 4 days\nFEE-26-6203 → Cash Control | $20,000.00 | age 9 days\n\nTRADES CONNECTED TO THE PERIOD\n• TRD-26-401: buy $1,125,000.00; 2026-06-21 trade / 2026-06-23 settlement; settled; Dealer Alpha\n• TRD-26-402: sell $560,000.00; 2026-06-23 trade / 2026-06-26 settlement; pending confirmation; Dealer Beta\n\nBOOK-TO-MARK INVENTORY\nInstrument | Lot | Position size | Accounting value | Market mark\n--- | --- | --- | --- | ---\nU.S. Treasury bill lot | TB-26-4103 | 1,750 | $1,667,500.00 | $1,676,500.00\nInvestment-grade bond lot | IG-26-7303 | 800 | $810,000.00 | $792,750.00\nOperating cash | CASH-26-8103 | 1 | $2,035,000.00 | $2,035,000.00\n\nAPPROVAL STATE\nOperations record completed by D. Foster at 2026-06-28T14:20:00Z. Reviewer: not assigned. Approval time: pending.\n\nQUERY:\nPrepare an identity and ownership verification brief for Blue Harbor Logistics Holdings LLC using only the supplied onboarding activity profile and operations break case record. The brief is for an internal compliance or onboarding reviewer and must distinguish evidence, procedure, result, and conclusion for each verification topic; define abbreviations on first use and avoid unexplained jargon.\n\nStructure the brief around the following named topics: entity identification and formation, ownership and control percentages, authorized actors and verification status, balance-sheet profile, and risk parameters and prohibited usage. For each topic, cite only the facts present in the two supplied records; any finding not supported by those records must be labeled `Not Determinable` rather than estimated or supplemented.\n\nReconcile the cash position across the two records. Match the recorded cash balance of $2,035,000.00 from the intake balance-sheet profile against the external cash of $2,085,000.00 in the operations reconciliation narrative. Match the documented $30,000.00 timing item and the $20,000.00 unresolved cash break by break reference and desk, calculate each difference, and retain any non-zero residual as `Unresolved`. Do not aggregate settled and pending items when determining reconciliation status.\n\nCalculate the liquidity headroom as the recorded cash balance of $2,035,000.00 minus the liquidity minimum of $1,119,250.00, showing both inputs and the resulting dollar amount. Then state whether the unresolved $20,000.00 cash break would reduce that headroom if confirmed.\n\nList each missing or unverified item under an `Open Evidence` section, including the absent secondary contact authority evidence, the absent current insurance certificate, the unverified Avery Chen finance-contact status, the pending confirmation for TRD-26-402, and the unassigned reviewer. For each open item, state which verification conclusion it prevents.\n\nFor each unresolved break or missing evidence item, state the affected population or account, the quantified exposure where the records supply an amount, the plausible operational or verification impact, and the evidence limitation that prevents closure. Distinguish quantified exposure from qualitative consequences that cannot be measured from the packet.\n\nUse only the exact labels `Verified`, `Unverified`, `Pending`, `Unresolved`, and `Not Determinable` for evidence and reconciliation status fields. Do not use `approved`, `closed`, or `reconciled` while a corresponding prerequisite remains missing or pending. Do not state that the operations record is approved, that the missing confirmation for TRD-26-402 is resolved, or that the cash reconciliation is clean while the reviewer is unassigned, approval is pending, and the $20,000.00 cash break remains unresolved.\n\nIdentify the required reviewer and approval prerequisite for the operations record. State that Marcus Vale is the only verified primary signer while Avery Chen is an unverified finance contact, and do not imply final approval while the reviewer is unassigned and approval time is pending.",
