    "full_prompt": "MATERIAL 1:\nCompanies overwhelmingly provided timely responses, providing a timely response to 99.6% of the more\nthan 5.9 million complaints sent to them for review in 2025.\n24\n24 Complaints in which a company did not provide a response within 15 calendar days of the complaint being sent to\nthe company—or within 60 days if it requested more time—are reflected in the Consumer Complaint Database as\nnot having received a timely response.15 BUREAU OF CONSUMER FINANCIAL PROTECTION\nTABLE 1: HOW COMPANIES HAVE RESPONDED TO CONSUMER COMPLAINTS\nFinancial product\nor service Closed with\nmonetary\nrelief\nClosed with\nnon-monetary\nrelief\nClosed with\nexplanation\nAdmin\nresponse\nCompany\nreviewing\nCompany\ndid not\nprovide a\ntimely\nresponse\nAll <1% 37% 53% 9% <1% <1%\nCredit or consumer\nreporting\n<1% 40% 51% 10% <1% <1%\nDebt collection <1% 23% 66% 7% <1% 3%\nCredit card 12% 19% 63% 5% <1% <1%\nChecking or savings 10% 5% 83% 1% <1% <1%\nMoney transfer or\nservice, virtual\ncurrency\n2% 2% 94% <1% <1% 1%\nMortgage 2% 3% 91% 3% <1% 1%\nVehicle loan or lease 2% 6% 88% 2% <1% 2%\nStudent loan <1% 1% 66% <1% 1% 31%\n25\nPersonal loan 3% 4% 86% 2% <1% 4%\nPrepaid card 14% 7% 71% 3% <1% 5%\nDebt or credit\nmanagement\n3% 10% 76% 3% <1% 8%\nPayday loan 2% 2% 86% 5% <1% 5%\nTitle loan 2% 6% 88% <1% <1% 3%\nDeposit advance 3% 2% 84% 3% <1% 8%\n25 See discussion infra Section 4.8.16 BUREAU OF CONSUMER FINANCIAL PROTECTION\n4. Complaint types\nThis section summarizes the types of complaints and issues identified by consumers in 2025.\n\nQUERY:\nPrepare a complaint response outcomes complaint issue classification brief using only the supplied CFPB annual report text and table. Begin with a one-sentence overview of the 2025 complaint response outcome distribution. Then classify each financial product or service row into the response-outcome categories defined in the table—Closed with monetary relief, Closed with non-monetary relief, Closed with explanation, Admin response, Company reviewing, and Company did not provide a timely response—using the percentages shown for that product. For every classification and comparison, identify the supporting material and the exact figure or outcome category used, and keep the source label beside each product row, percentage, and timing status. Compare each financial product or service against the All-products row using the same outcome categories and percentage basis, and rank the products by their percentage of Closed with explanation from highest to lowest. Show every percentage with exactly two decimal places and order the product rows by the Closed with explanation percentage from highest to lowest. Apply the 15-calendar-day response window, extended to 60 days when a company requested more time, to the 2025 complaint review period and state which timing status the report assigns to complaints that missed the applicable window. Use only the supplied materials and label any product category, outcome percentage, or timeliness status not present in the materials as Not Determinable. Keep the brief to no more than 400 words and end with a next-step line identifying which product category shows the largest departure from the All-products pattern.",
