    "full_prompt": "MATERIAL 1:\nONBOARDING ACTIVITY PROFILE\n\nObserved relationship as at 2026-04-15\n\nRECENT FLOWS FIRST\nObserved on | Payment rail | Amount | Counterparty description\n--- | --- | --- | ---\n2026-04-03 | incoming ACH | $279,500.00 | customer receipts batch\n2026-04-06 | domestic wire | $134,700.00 | equipment supplier\n2026-04-11 | international wire | $55,500.00 | overseas vendor\n\nEXPECTED PATTERN\nMonthly credits $3,826,666.67; monthly debits $3,482,266.67; domestic wires 39; international wires 6. Products requested: operating cash management, credit facility review, investment-policy reporting. Anticipated source: operating revenue and documented owner equity.\n\nWHO THE CLIENT IS\nBlue Harbor Logistics Holdings LLC was formed in Virginia on 2009-05-26 and operates in regional freight and warehousing. Tax identifier: XX-XXX0010. Principal location: 231 Commerce Way, Suite 203, Virginia.\n\nWHO CONTROLS IT\n— Marcus Vale holds 44.0% and acts as Chief Executive Officer.\n— Iris Chen holds 36.0% and acts as Chief Operating Officer.\n— Harbor Employee Trust holds 20.0% and acts as Employee trust.\n\nWHO MAY ACT\n— Marcus Vale: primary signer (verified).\n— Avery Chen: finance contact only (not verified).\n\nBALANCE-SHEET PROFILE\nCash / A/R / inventory: $2,035,000.00 / $8,420,000.00 / $640,000.00\nSenior debt: $11,700,000.00\nAnnual revenue / EBITDA: $45,920,000.00 / $4,010,000.00\n\nRISK PARAMETERS\nBusiness objective: fleet replacement and consolidation of equipment notes\nLiquidity minimum: $1,119,250.00\nRisk setting: moderate\nProhibited usage: cryptocurrency transfers, bearer instruments, undocumented third-party payments\nMonitoring note: Fuel surcharge recovery lagged diesel-cost changes by an average of 43 days in Q4 2025.\n\nSUPPORTING FILES\ncertificate of formation—present, 2009-05-26; ownership schedule—present, 2025-12-31; 2025 financial statements—present, 2025-12-31; secondary contact authority evidence—absent; current insurance certificate—absent\n\nMATERIAL 2:\nOPERATIONS BREAK CASE RECORD\n\nCase entity: Blue Harbor Logistics Holdings LLC\nPosition date: 2026-06-27\n\nOPEN CASES\nBreak reference | Finding | Amount at risk | Open since | Desk | Backup\n--- | --- | --- | --- | --- | ---\nEX-26-401 | cash break | $20,000.00 | 2026-06-26 | Cash Control | received\nEX-26-402 | missing confirmation | $560,000.00 | 2026-06-24 | Trade Support | not received\n\nRECONCILIATION NARRATIVE\nExternal cash of $2,085,000.00 exceeds recorded cash of $2,035,000.00. A $30,000.00 timing item is documented, leaving $20,000.00 unresolved.\n\nDIFFERENCE OWNERSHIP\nDEP-26-5103 → Treasury Operations | $30,000.00 | age 4 days\nFEE-26-6203 → Cash Control | $20,000.00 | age 9 days\n\nTRADES CONNECTED TO THE PERIOD\n• TRD-26-401: buy $1,125,000.00; 2026-06-21 trade / 2026-06-23 settlement; settled; Dealer Alpha\n• TRD-26-402: sell $560,000.00; 2026-06-23 trade / 2026-06-26 settlement; pending confirmation; Dealer Beta\n\nBOOK-TO-MARK INVENTORY\nInstrument | Lot | Position size | Accounting value | Market mark\n--- | --- | --- | --- | ---\nU.S. Treasury bill lot | TB-26-4103 | 1,750 | $1,667,500.00 | $1,676,500.00\nInvestment-grade bond lot | IG-26-7303 | 800 | $810,000.00 | $792,750.00\nOperating cash | CASH-26-8103 | 1 | $2,035,000.00 | $2,035,000.00\n\nAPPROVAL STATE\nOperations record completed by D. Foster at 2026-06-28T14:20:00Z. Reviewer: not assigned. Approval time: pending.\n\nQUERY:\nPrepare a Blue Harbor Logistics Holdings LLC missing onboarding evidence review brief that integrates the ONBOARDING ACTIVITY PROFILE observed as at 2026-04-15 with the OPERATIONS BREAK CASE RECORD positioned at 2026-06-27. Begin with a one-sentence readiness statement indicating whether the onboarding record can be treated as complete based on the evidence status described below. Use only these two supplied records; where a needed input is absent or unverified, label the result `Not Determinable` and do not estimate it.\n\nPresent the review as a table with columns `Review area`, `Source record`, `Evidence status`, `Unresolved difference`, and `Required action`. Cover the following review areas as distinct topics, each mapped to its exact source figure or rule: ownership and control, authorized actors, balance-sheet profile, risk parameters, and supporting-file status. For every finding, numeric input, and resulting decision, keep the source record label beside the item; do not use end-only citations.\n\nReconcile the recorded cash balance of $2,035,000.00 in the intake balance-sheet profile against the external cash of $2,085,000.00 in the operations reconciliation narrative and the documented $30,000.00 timing item. Calculate the unresolved cash difference as external cash minus recorded cash minus the documented timing item, showing all three inputs and the resulting difference in U.S. dollars, and retain any non-zero remainder as `Unresolved` rather than marking the cash position reconciled.\n\nFor each open item, including the cash break EX-26-401, the missing confirmation EX-26-402, the absent secondary contact authority evidence, and the absent current insurance certificate, state the affected exposure or population, the plausible impact, and any evidence limitation that prevents quantification. For each such item, specify the corrective action, the responsible desk or owner, and the evidence required to close it.\n\nDo not mark the onboarding record as complete or the operations record as approved while required evidence is missing or unverified. For each decision, show the active evidence from the intake or operations record, the governing review standard, and the resulting action as one connected chain rather than as disconnected fragments. Close with a `Next action:` line tied to the highest-priority unresolved finding.",
