    "full_prompt": "MATERIAL 1:\nONBOARDING ACTIVITY PROFILE\n\nObserved relationship as at 2026-04-15\n\nRECENT FLOWS FIRST\nObserved on | Payment rail | Amount | Counterparty description\n--- | --- | --- | ---\n2026-04-03 | incoming ACH | $279,500.00 | customer receipts batch\n2026-04-06 | domestic wire | $134,700.00 | equipment supplier\n2026-04-11 | international wire | $55,500.00 | overseas vendor\n\nEXPECTED PATTERN\nMonthly credits $3,826,666.67; monthly debits $3,482,266.67; domestic wires 39; international wires 6. Products requested: operating cash management, credit facility review, investment-policy reporting. Anticipated source: operating revenue and documented owner equity.\n\nWHO THE CLIENT IS\nBlue Harbor Logistics Holdings LLC was formed in Virginia on 2009-05-26 and operates in regional freight and warehousing. Tax identifier: XX-XXX0010. Principal location: 231 Commerce Way, Suite 203, Virginia.\n\nWHO CONTROLS IT\n— Marcus Vale holds 44.0% and acts as Chief Executive Officer.\n— Iris Chen holds 36.0% and acts as Chief Operating Officer.\n— Harbor Employee Trust holds 20.0% and acts as Employee trust.\n\nWHO MAY ACT\n— Marcus Vale: primary signer (verified).\n— Avery Chen: finance contact only (not verified).\n\nBALANCE-SHEET PROFILE\nCash / A/R / inventory: $2,035,000.00 / $8,420,000.00 / $640,000.00\nSenior debt: $11,700,000.00\nAnnual revenue / EBITDA: $45,920,000.00 / $4,010,000.00\n\nRISK PARAMETERS\nBusiness objective: fleet replacement and consolidation of equipment notes\nLiquidity minimum: $1,119,250.00\nRisk setting: moderate\nProhibited usage: cryptocurrency transfers, bearer instruments, undocumented third-party payments\nMonitoring note: Fuel surcharge recovery lagged diesel-cost changes by an average of 43 days in Q4 2025.\n\nSUPPORTING FILES\ncertificate of formation—present, 2009-05-26; ownership schedule—present, 2025-12-31; 2025 financial statements—present, 2025-12-31; secondary contact authority evidence—absent; current insurance certificate—absent\n\nMATERIAL 2:\nTRANSACTION DESK SNAPSHOT\n\nBlue Harbor Logistics Holdings LLC | proposed close: 2030-09-30\n\nSTRUCTURE AT A GLANCE\nDELAYED-DRAW TERM LOAN / $9,500,000.00 / SOFR + 3.40%\nPurpose — fleet replacement and consolidation of equipment notes\nSponsor amount identified — $2,250,000.00\n\nLEVERAGE READOUT\nLatest revenue change: -2.92%\nFully drawn debt: $21,200,000.00\nPro forma leverage: 5.29x\n\nTWO-YEAR ACTUALS\nYear | Turnover | EBITDA | Interest paid | Capex\n--- | --- | --- | --- | ---\nFY2024 | $47,300,000.00 | $3,548,672.57 | $830,700.00 | $2,033,900.00\nFY2025 | $45,920,000.00 | $4,010,000.00 | $865,800.00 | $2,112,320.00\n\nASSET COVERAGE NOTES\n• $2,035,000.00 cash\n• $6,904,400.00 preliminary eligible receivables\n• $640,000.00 inventory at book\n• $5,415,000.00 equipment value (2025-12-30)\n\nBASE PROJECTION\nFY2026: $49,593,600.00 revenue / $4,290,700.00 EBITDA | FY2027: $52,808,000.00 revenue / $4,651,600.00 EBITDA | FY2028: $56,022,400.00 revenue / $5,012,500.00 EBITDA\n\nBREAK CASE\nAt 15.0% below base revenue and 3.5 points of margin compression, EBITDA is $2,526,300.00. Management's response remains unverified: Hiring pause and reduction of discretionary capital expenditure; not independently verified.\n\nITEMS NOT CLEARED\n— Confirm payoff amount for existing senior debt.\n— Validate the latest accounts-receivable aging against the general ledger.\n— Fuel surcharge recovery lagged diesel-cost changes by an average of 43 days in Q4 2025.\n— Obtain evidence for any sponsor support shown in the request.\n\nQUERY:\nPrepare a Blue Harbor Logistics Holdings LLC onboarding record authorized contact review brief that reconciles the ONBOARDING ACTIVITY PROFILE observed as at 2026-04-15 with the TRANSACTION DESK SNAPSHOT for the proposed delayed-draw term loan closing 2030-09-30. Address the brief to a compliance reviewer in neutral, formal language, and pair every contact authority determination with the specific source record and as-of date that supports it. Use only the two supplied records; do not add external facts, market data, customary practice, or assumptions, and label any result that cannot be established from those records as `Not Determinable`. Cover, as distinct topics, the named contact roles, ownership and control percentages, the requested products, the liquidity minimum, and the prohibited-usage restrictions. For contact authority and supporting-file status fields, use only the exact labels `Verified`, `Not verified`, `Absent`, and `Not Determinable`, and do not use the words `approved`, `cleared`, or `confirmed` for any item whose prerequisite evidence is missing. Identify the specific issues relevant to the authorized contact review, including the unverified finance-contact-only role, the absent secondary contact authority evidence, the absent current insurance certificate, and the unresolved transaction desk items such as the unconfirmed senior debt payoff and the unverified management response, and classify each as confirmed, unresolved, or dependent on missing evidence. Reconcile the observed recent payment flows against the expected monthly credit and debit pattern, matching by payment rail and period where the records allow, calculate each difference, and retain any non-zero or unmatched item as `Unresolved`; do not aggregate settled and pending amounts. Compare the base projection and the break case as alternative scenarios for the proposed facility, stating the changed assumption, the resulting EBITDA, and the decision implication, while keeping the management response unverified status separate. Apply the supplied 15.0% revenue reduction and 3.5 percentage point margin compression to the base projection, showing the changed assumption, source inputs, resulting EBITDA, and a comparison with the liquidity minimum and pro forma leverage readout. List the supporting records reviewed and the documents still required, including the certificate of formation, ownership schedule, 2025 financial statements, secondary contact authority evidence, current insurance certificate, and evidence for sponsor support, and identify which are present, absent, or unverified as of their stated dates. Finally, apply this conditional action rule to the authorized contact review: if the secondary contact authority evidence remains absent, assign the status `Hold for evidence` and state what must be supplied to resume; otherwise the contact may proceed only as a finance-contact-only role.",
