    "full_prompt": "MATERIAL 1:\nEntity: CATERPILLAR INC\nINCOME STATEMENT (USD, annual 10-K values)\nConcept (as reported) | FY end 2021-12-31 | FY end 2022-12-31 | FY end 2023-12-31 | FY end 2024-12-31 | FY end 2025-12-31\n--- | --- | --- | --- | --- | ---\nRevenues | 50,971,000,000 | 59,427,000,000 | 67,060,000,000 | 64,809,000,000 | 67,589,000,000\nCostOfRevenue | 35,513,000,000 | 41,350,000,000 | 42,767,000,000 | 40,199,000,000 | 44,752,000,000\nCostOfGoodsAndServicesSold | — | 413,000,000 | 160,000,000 | 33,000,000 | 49,000,000\nOperatingIncomeLoss | 6,878,000,000 | 7,904,000,000 | 12,966,000,000 | 13,072,000,000 | 11,151,000,000\nIncomeTaxExpenseBenefit | 1,742,000,000 | 2,067,000,000 | 2,781,000,000 | 2,629,000,000 | 2,768,000,000\nResearchAndDevelopmentExpense | 1,686,000,000 | 1,814,000,000 | 2,108,000,000 | 2,107,000,000 | 2,148,000,000\nEarningsPerShareBasic (USD/shares) | 11.93 | 12.72 | 20.24 | 22.17 | 18.9\n\nMATERIAL 2:\nEntity: CATERPILLAR INC\nBALANCE SHEET (USD, annual 10-K values)\nConcept (as reported) | FY end 2021-12-31 | FY end 2022-12-31 | FY end 2023-12-31 | FY end 2024-12-31 | FY end 2025-12-31\n--- | --- | --- | --- | --- | ---\nAssets | 82,793,000,000 | 81,943,000,000 | 87,476,000,000 | 87,764,000,000 | 98,585,000,000\nLiabilities | 66,277,000,000 | 66,052,000,000 | 67,973,000,000 | 68,270,000,000 | 77,267,000,000\nStockholdersEquityOther | -35,000,000 | -44,000,000 | -4,000,000 | 2,000,000 | 5,000,000\nAssetsCurrent | 43,455,000,000 | 43,785,000,000 | 46,949,000,000 | 45,682,000,000 | 52,485,000,000\nLiabilitiesCurrent | 29,847,000,000 | 31,531,000,000 | 34,728,000,000 | 32,272,000,000 | 36,558,000,000\nCashAndCashEquivalentsAtCarryingValue | 9,254,000,000 | 7,004,000,000 | 6,978,000,000 | 6,889,000,000 | 9,980,000,000\nAccountsReceivableNetCurrent | 8,477,000,000 | 8,856,000,000 | 9,310,000,000 | 9,282,000,000 | 10,920,000,000\nInventoryNet | 14,038,000,000 | 16,270,000,000 | 16,565,000,000 | 16,827,000,000 | 18,135,000,000\nLongTermDebtNoncurrent | 26,033,000,000 | 25,714,000,000 | 24,472,000,000 | 27,351,000,000 | 30,696,000,000\n\nMATERIAL 3:\nEntity: CATERPILLAR INC\nCASH FLOW (USD, annual 10-K values)\nConcept (as reported) | FY end 2021-12-31 | FY end 2022-12-31 | FY end 2023-12-31 | FY end 2024-12-31 | FY end 2025-12-31\n--- | --- | --- | --- | --- | ---\nNetCashProvidedByUsedInOperatingActivities | 7,198,000,000 | 7,766,000,000 | 12,885,000,000 | 12,035,000,000 | 11,739,000,000\nNetCashProvidedByUsedInInvestingActivities | -3,084,000,000 | -2,541,000,000 | -5,871,000,000 | -2,453,000,000 | -4,707,000,000\nNetCashProvidedByUsedInFinancingActivities | -4,188,000,000 | -7,281,000,000 | -6,932,000,000 | -9,565,000,000 | -3,899,000,000\nPaymentsToAcquirePropertyPlantAndEquipment | 1,093,000,000 | 1,296,000,000 | 1,597,000,000 | 1,988,000,000 | 2,821,000,000\n\nQUERY:\nPrepare a financial statement linkage brief for Caterpillar Inc. using only the supplied income statement, balance sheet, and cash-flow statement data for fiscal years ended 2021-12-31 through 2025-12-31. The brief must contain four level-2 headings in this exact order: `Source Evidence`, `Linkage Calculations`, `Cross-Statement Analysis`, and `Open Items`.\n\nWrite for a financial reporting reviewer: distinguish reported evidence, derived calculations, linkage tests, and open items in each section, and define any financial terminology on first use.\n\nUse only the supplied materials. Do not add external market data, industry benchmarks, or assumptions. Label any linkage result that cannot be established from the provided figures as `Not Determinable`.\n\nIn the `Source Evidence` section, map every linkage finding to the specific statement, concept line, fiscal year, and reported figure used, with a source label beside each input, calculation, and conclusion. Preserve all reported figures, concept labels, fiscal-year dates, signs, and units exactly as they appear in the supplied statements, and do not round or relabel any source value before completing the linkage tests.\n\nIn the `Linkage Calculations` section, complete the following calculations for each fiscal year, showing the numerator, denominator, and units for each:\n1. Gross margin percentage as Revenues minus CostOfRevenue divided by Revenues, using the income statement figures.\n2. Current ratio as AssetsCurrent divided by LiabilitiesCurrent, using the balance sheet figures.\n3. Independently recalculate the change in CashAndCashEquivalentsAtCarryingValue from the balance sheet for each fiscal year and compare it against the sum of NetCashProvidedByUsedInOperatingActivities, NetCashProvidedByUsedInInvestingActivities, and NetCashProvidedByUsedInFinancingActivities from the cash-flow statement, showing the variance for each year.\n\nIn the `Cross-Statement Analysis` section, apply the as-of date 2025-12-31 consistently as the single reporting endpoint for all five fiscal-year comparisons across the income statement, balance sheet, and cash-flow statement, and flag any period misalignment between the three statements.\n\nIn the `Open Items` section, list any linkage result that cannot be established from the provided figures as `Not Determinable`, and identify any unresolved variance or period misalignment.\n\nUse only the exact terminology `Ties`, `Variance`, and `Not Determinable` when reporting each linkage result, and do not use the words `reconciled` or `approved` unless the underlying calculation ties out exactly.",
