    "full_prompt": "MATERIAL 1:\nEntity: DELTA AIR LINES, INC.\nINCOME STATEMENT (USD, annual 10-K values)\nConcept (as reported) | FY end 2021-12-31 | FY end 2022-12-31 | FY end 2023-12-31 | FY end 2024-12-31 | FY end 2025-12-31\n--- | --- | --- | --- | --- | ---\nRevenueFromContractWithCustomerExcludingAssessedTax | 29,899,000,000 | 50,582,000,000 | 58,048,000,000 | 61,643,000,000 | 63,364,000,000\nOperatingIncomeLoss | 1,886,000,000 | 3,661,000,000 | 5,521,000,000 | 5,995,000,000 | 5,822,000,000\nNetIncomeLoss | 280,000,000 | 1,318,000,000 | 4,609,000,000 | 3,457,000,000 | 5,005,000,000\nIncomeTaxExpenseBenefit | 118,000,000 | 596,000,000 | 999,000,000 | 1,201,000,000 | 1,180,000,000\nEarningsPerShareBasic (USD/shares) | 0.44 | 2.07 | 7.21 | 5.39 | 7.72\n\nQUERY:\nPrepare a profitability driver evidence brief for Delta Air Lines, Inc. using only the supplied annual income statement data for fiscal years ended 2021-12-31 through 2025-12-31. Organize the brief into the following sections in this order: `Scope and Source`, `Driver Evidence`, `Margin Analysis`, `Year-over-Year Movement`, and `Conclusion`.\n\nWrite for a financial analysis reviewer who needs to trace every claim back to the underlying disclosure. In the `Scope and Source` section, state that the brief relies solely on the supplied Delta Air Lines income statement figures and identify the reporting entity, the concept labels as reported, the fiscal-year-end dates, and the units (USD for income statement amounts; USD/shares for basic EPS). Preserve the reported figures, dates, concept names, and units exactly as disclosed; do not round, relabel, or restate any source value before completing the analysis.\n\nIn the `Driver Evidence` section, identify the profitability drivers observable from the disclosed lines: RevenueFromContractWithCustomerExcludingAssessedTax, OperatingIncomeLoss, NetIncomeLoss, IncomeTaxExpenseBenefit, and EarningsPerShareBasic. For each driver observation, cite the specific income statement line and the fiscal year from which the figure was taken, and keep the source label beside every figure used.\n\nIn the `Margin Analysis` section, compute two ratios for each fiscal year: operating margin as OperatingIncomeLoss divided by RevenueFromContractWithCustomerExcludingAssessedTax, and net margin as NetIncomeLoss divided by RevenueFromContractWithCustomerExcludingAssessedTax. Show the source inputs for each calculation with their fiscal-year labels and express each margin as a percentage to one decimal place. Do not supply the final margin values in this instruction; the brief must derive and present them from the disclosed figures.\n\nIn the `Year-over-Year Movement` section, apply the disclosed fiscal-year-end windows consistently. For each driver line and each computed margin, calculate the year-over-year change for each adjacent pair of fiscal years (2021-12-31 to 2022-12-31, 2022-12-31 to 2023-12-31, 2023-12-31 to 2024-12-31, and 2024-12-31 to 2025-12-31). Label every change with the exact source fiscal-year windows being compared and state whether the movement is an increase or decrease. Keep reported figures separate from computed changes and do not treat a computed change as a disclosed value.\n\nIn the `Conclusion` section, synthesize the driver evidence, margin results, and year-over-year movements to state which disclosed lines most explain the observed profitability pattern across the five fiscal years. Ground every conclusion in the cited income statement lines and computed results. If any driver conclusion cannot be established from the supplied data alone, mark it `Not Determinable` rather than supplementing with outside facts or assumptions.",
