    "full_prompt": "MATERIAL 1:\nEntity: Exxon Mobil Corporation\nBALANCE SHEET (USD, annual 10-K values)\nConcept (as reported) | FY end 2021-12-31 | FY end 2022-12-31 | FY end 2023-12-31 | FY end 2024-12-31 | FY end 2025-12-31\n--- | --- | --- | --- | --- | ---\nAssets | 338,923,000,000 | 369,067,000,000 | 376,317,000,000 | 453,475,000,000 | 448,980,000,000\nLiabilities | 163,240,000,000 | 166,594,000,000 | 163,779,000,000 | 182,869,000,000 | 182,354,000,000\nStockholdersEquity | 168,577,000,000 | 195,049,000,000 | 204,802,000,000 | 263,705,000,000 | 259,386,000,000\nAssetsCurrent | 59,154,000,000 | 97,631,000,000 | 96,609,000,000 | 91,990,000,000 | 83,382,000,000\nLiabilitiesCurrent | 56,643,000,000 | 69,045,000,000 | 65,316,000,000 | 70,307,000,000 | 72,330,000,000\nCashAndCashEquivalentsAtCarryingValue | 6,802,000,000 | 29,640,000,000 | 31,539,000,000 | 23,029,000,000 | 10,681,000,000\nAccountsReceivableNetCurrent | 26,883,000,000 | 32,844,000,000 | 30,296,000,000 | 35,282,000,000 | 35,744,000,000\nLongTermDebtCurrent | 2,392,000,000 | 181,000,000 | 4,009,000,000 | 4,892,000,000 | 6,200,000,000\nOtherLiabilitiesNoncurrent | 21,717,000,000 | 21,733,000,000 | — | — | —\n\nQUERY:\nPrepare a balance sheet structure analysis brief for Exxon Mobil Corporation using only the supplied annual balance sheet disclosures for fiscal years ended 2021-12-31 through 2025-12-31. Write the brief for an internal credit or investment analyst reviewer: define each ratio formula on first use, avoid unexplained abbreviations, and pair every structural observation with the specific balance sheet line items that support it.\n\nFrom the reported figures, calculate for each fiscal year-end the debt-to-equity ratio, defined as total Liabilities divided by total StockholdersEquity, and the current ratio, defined as AssetsCurrent divided by LiabilitiesCurrent. Present these ratios and the underlying reported amounts in a Markdown table with the columns Fiscal Year-End, Total Assets, Total Liabilities, Stockholders Equity, Debt-to-Equity Ratio, Current Ratio, and Tie-Out Status.\n\nIndependently verify the accounting identity Assets = Liabilities + StockholdersEquity for each fiscal year-end. For each year, show the recalculated total of Liabilities plus StockholdersEquity, the reported Total Assets figure, the variance between the recalculated total and the reported Total Assets, and state whether that year ties out. Preserve the exact reported USD amounts, fiscal year-end dates, and line-item names from the source without rounding or relabeling them, and keep reported figures separate from any recalculated totals.\n\nApply the FY-end as-of dates consistently across the five-year series, label each observation with its exact fiscal year-end date, and flag any year where a reported line item is missing for that period. Treat the missing OtherLiabilitiesNoncurrent values for FY2023, FY2024, and FY2025 as unresolved gaps: list them under an Open Evidence section and state which structural ratio or comparison they prevent from being completed.\n\nFor every ratio, tie-out result, and structural observation, identify the supporting balance sheet line item and the exact fiscal year-end from the source, keeping the source label beside each numeric input and derived result. Use only the supplied disclosures; do not add external market data, customary practice, or facts remembered from outside the packet. Where a needed input is absent, preserve the missing status rather than estimating it, and label any ratio or comparison that cannot be established from the supplied figures as Not Determinable.",
