    "full_prompt": "MATERIAL 1:\nEntity: CVS HEALTH CORPORATION\nBALANCE SHEET (USD, annual 10-K values)\nConcept (as reported) | FY end 2021-12-31 | FY end 2022-12-31 | FY end 2023-12-31 | FY end 2024-12-31 | FY end 2025-12-31\n--- | --- | --- | --- | --- | ---\nAssets | 232,999,000,000 | 228,275,000,000 | 249,728,000,000 | 253,215,000,000 | 253,538,000,000\nLiabilities | 157,618,000,000 | 156,506,000,000 | 173,092,000,000 | 177,485,000,000 | 178,156,000,000\nStockholdersEquity | 75,075,000,000 | 71,469,000,000 | 76,461,000,000 | 75,560,000,000 | 75,214,000,000\nAssetsCurrent | 60,008,000,000 | 65,633,000,000 | 67,858,000,000 | 68,645,000,000 | 74,714,000,000\nLiabilitiesCurrent | 67,807,000,000 | 69,421,000,000 | 79,189,000,000 | 84,609,000,000 | 88,692,000,000\nCashAndCashEquivalentsAtCarryingValue | 9,408,000,000 | 12,945,000,000 | 8,196,000,000 | 8,586,000,000 | 8,453,000,000\nAccountsReceivableNetCurrent | 24,431,000,000 | 27,276,000,000 | 35,227,000,000 | 36,469,000,000 | 39,779,000,000\nInventoryNet | 17,760,000,000 | 19,090,000,000 | 18,025,000,000 | 18,107,000,000 | 19,246,000,000\nOtherLiabilitiesNoncurrent | 1,904,000,000 | 6,730,000,000 | 6,211,000,000 | 5,431,000,000 | 4,777,000,000\n\nMATERIAL 2:\nEntity: CVS HEALTH CORPORATION\nINCOME STATEMENT (USD, annual 10-K values)\nConcept (as reported) | FY end 2021-12-31 | FY end 2022-12-31 | FY end 2023-12-31 | FY end 2024-12-31 | FY end 2025-12-31\n--- | --- | --- | --- | --- | ---\nRevenues | 292,111,000,000 | 322,467,000,000 | 357,776,000,000 | 372,809,000,000 | 402,067,000,000\nRelatedPartyTransactionOtherRevenuesFromTransactionsWithRelatedParty | 79,000,000 | 87,000,000 | — | — | —\nCostOfGoodsAndServicesSold | 175,803,000,000 | 196,892,000,000 | 217,098,000,000 | 206,287,000,000 | 221,167,000,000\nOperatingIncomeLoss | 13,310,000,000 | 7,954,000,000 | 13,743,000,000 | 8,516,000,000 | 4,660,000,000\nNetIncomeLoss | 8,001,000,000 | 4,311,000,000 | 8,344,000,000 | 4,614,000,000 | 1,768,000,000\nIncomeTaxExpenseBenefit | 2,548,000,000 | 1,509,000,000 | 2,805,000,000 | 1,562,000,000 | 408,000,000\nEarningsPerShareBasic (USD/shares) | 6.07 | 3.29 | 6.49 | 3.67 | 1.4\n\nQUERY:\nPrepare a capital allocation evidence brief for CVS Health Corporation using only the supplied annual 10-K income statement and balance sheet figures for FY end 2021-12-31 through FY end 2025-12-31. The brief must integrate the two statements into one cross-statement analysis rather than describing each statement separately. Structure the brief with the following sections in this order: Opening Conclusion, Evidence Scope and Period Alignment, Ratio Analysis, Tie-Out Verification, Missing and Unresolved Evidence, and Next Action. Write for a capital allocation review audience: define any derived metric on first use, and pair every trend or tie-out observation with the governing reported line item and fiscal period. Open the brief with a one-sentence capital allocation evidence conclusion, and close with a single next-action line tied to the most material unresolved evidence item or cross-statement discrepancy identified in the analysis. Use only the supplied materials; do not introduce external benchmarks, industry averages, or assumptions, and label any conclusion that cannot be established from the two statements as Not Determinable. Preserve all reported figures, concept labels, fiscal endpoints, and units exactly as they appear in the two statements, including the dash entries for the related-party revenue line; do not round, relabel, or convert any reported value before performing a calculation or comparison. In the Evidence Scope and Period Alignment section, confirm that every income statement and balance sheet figure used in the brief carries the same fiscal endpoint, and identify any period misalignment or missing endpoint before combining figures across the two statements. In the Ratio Analysis section, calculate, for each aligned fiscal year from FY end 2021-12-31 through FY end 2025-12-31, the return on average stockholders' equity using the reported NetIncomeLoss from the income statement as the numerator and the average of the current and immediately preceding year-end StockholdersEquity from the balance sheet as the denominator, expressed as a percentage to two decimal places. In the Tie-Out Verification section, independently verify the reported Assets, Liabilities, and StockholdersEquity for each fiscal year by recalculating the accounting identity Assets minus Liabilities equals StockholdersEquity from the reported balance sheet line items; show the recalculated equity, the variance from the reported StockholdersEquity, and whether each year ties out. In the Missing and Unresolved Evidence section, treat the dash entries for RelatedPartyTransactionOtherRevenuesFromTransactionsWithRelatedParty in FY end 2023-12-31, FY end 2024-12-31, and FY end 2025-12-31 as missing values, label them as unresolved rather than zero, and state which capital allocation assessment or cross-statement check each missing value prevents. Throughout the brief, map every calculated ratio, tie-out result, trend observation, and unresolved item to the specific statement and reported line item used, keeping source labels beside each input and result rather than relying on end-only citations.",
