    "full_prompt": "MATERIAL 1:\nEntity: Exxon Mobil Corporation\nBALANCE SHEET (USD, annual 10-K values)\nConcept (as reported) | FY end 2021-12-31 | FY end 2022-12-31 | FY end 2023-12-31 | FY end 2024-12-31 | FY end 2025-12-31\n--- | --- | --- | --- | --- | ---\nAssets | 338,923,000,000 | 369,067,000,000 | 376,317,000,000 | 453,475,000,000 | 448,980,000,000\nLiabilities | 163,240,000,000 | 166,594,000,000 | 163,779,000,000 | 182,869,000,000 | 182,354,000,000\nStockholdersEquity | 168,577,000,000 | 195,049,000,000 | 204,802,000,000 | 263,705,000,000 | 259,386,000,000\nAssetsCurrent | 59,154,000,000 | 97,631,000,000 | 96,609,000,000 | 91,990,000,000 | 83,382,000,000\nLiabilitiesCurrent | 56,643,000,000 | 69,045,000,000 | 65,316,000,000 | 70,307,000,000 | 72,330,000,000\nCashAndCashEquivalentsAtCarryingValue | 6,802,000,000 | 29,640,000,000 | 31,539,000,000 | 23,029,000,000 | 10,681,000,000\nAccountsReceivableNetCurrent | 26,883,000,000 | 32,844,000,000 | 30,296,000,000 | 35,282,000,000 | 35,744,000,000\nLongTermDebtCurrent | 2,392,000,000 | 181,000,000 | 4,009,000,000 | 4,892,000,000 | 6,200,000,000\nOtherLiabilitiesNoncurrent | 21,717,000,000 | 21,733,000,000 | — | — | —\n\nMATERIAL 2:\nEntity: Exxon Mobil Corporation\nINCOME STATEMENT (USD, annual 10-K values)\nConcept (as reported) | FY end 2021-12-31 | FY end 2022-12-31 | FY end 2023-12-31 | FY end 2024-12-31 | FY end 2025-12-31\n--- | --- | --- | --- | --- | ---\nRevenues | 285,640,000,000 | 413,680,000,000 | 344,582,000,000 | 349,585,000,000 | 332,238,000,000\nNetIncomeLoss | 23,040,000,000 | 55,740,000,000 | 36,010,000,000 | 33,680,000,000 | 28,844,000,000\nIncomeTaxExpenseBenefit | 7,636,000,000 | 20,176,000,000 | 15,429,000,000 | 13,810,000,000 | 11,504,000,000\nResearchAndDevelopmentExpense | 843,000,000 | 824,000,000 | 900,000,000 | 1,000,000,000 | 1,200,000,000\nEarningsPerShareBasic (USD/shares) | 5.39 | 13.26 | 8.89 | 7.84 | 6.7\n\nQUERY:\nProduce a capital allocation evidence brief for Exxon Mobil Corporation that integrates the supplied income statement and balance sheet evidence across the five aligned fiscal years ending 2021-12-31 through 2025-12-31. Write the brief for an audit reviewer, distinguishing evidence, procedure, result, and conclusion for each cross-statement analysis.\n\nUse only the supplied Exxon Mobil income statement and balance sheet materials. Do not introduce outside facts, external assumptions, or customary practice. Label any result that cannot be established from the supplied materials as Not Determinable.\n\nFor every extracted figure, calculated input, and derived result, identify the supporting material and the exact concept and fiscal-year figure used. Keep source labels beside each numeric input and result; end-only citations are insufficient.\n\nPreserve the exact reported figures, concept labels, units, and fiscal-year endpoints from both statements wherever they control a result or comparison. Do not round source values before completing a calculation or verification.\n\nApply the aligned fiscal-year endpoints consistently across every year-over-year comparison and calculation, and state the applicable period for each result.\n\nFor each fiscal year, calculate the following using only the reported concepts from the two statements, showing the formula and inputs for each: net income margin as NetIncomeLoss divided by Revenues; effective tax rate as IncomeTaxExpenseBenefit divided by the sum of NetIncomeLoss and IncomeTaxExpenseBenefit; asset turnover as Revenues divided by Assets; and return on equity as NetIncomeLoss divided by StockholdersEquity.\n\nIndependently verify the reported StockholdersEquity for each fiscal year by recalculating it as Assets minus Liabilities from the balance sheet. Show the reported value, the recalculated value, and any variance. Use only Pass, Fail, and Missing Evidence in the verification status field for each recalculated balance-sheet item.\n\nFor the missing OtherLiabilitiesNoncurrent values in fiscal years 2023, 2024, and 2025, mark each absence as unresolved under an Open Evidence section and state which balance-sheet-derived calculation or conclusion it prevents. Do not infer a zero value or a clean reconciliation for those missing items.\n\nClose the brief with a single-sentence readiness gate stating which evidence, if any, remains insufficient to support the capital allocation analysis.",
