    "full_prompt": "MATERIAL 1:\nTRANSACTION DESK SNAPSHOT\n\nBlue Harbor Logistics Holdings LLC | proposed close: 2030-09-30\n\nSTRUCTURE AT A GLANCE\nDELAYED-DRAW TERM LOAN / $9,500,000.00 / SOFR + 3.40%\nPurpose — fleet replacement and consolidation of equipment notes\nSponsor amount identified — $2,250,000.00\n\nLEVERAGE READOUT\nLatest revenue change: -2.92%\nFully drawn debt: $21,200,000.00\nPro forma leverage: 5.29x\n\nTWO-YEAR ACTUALS\nYear | Turnover | EBITDA | Interest paid | Capex\n--- | --- | --- | --- | ---\nFY2024 | $47,300,000.00 | $3,548,672.57 | $830,700.00 | $2,033,900.00\nFY2025 | $45,920,000.00 | $4,010,000.00 | $865,800.00 | $2,112,320.00\n\nASSET COVERAGE NOTES\n• $2,035,000.00 cash\n• $6,904,400.00 preliminary eligible receivables\n• $640,000.00 inventory at book\n• $5,415,000.00 equipment value (2025-12-30)\n\nBASE PROJECTION\nFY2026: $49,593,600.00 revenue / $4,290,700.00 EBITDA | FY2027: $52,808,000.00 revenue / $4,651,600.00 EBITDA | FY2028: $56,022,400.00 revenue / $5,012,500.00 EBITDA\n\nBREAK CASE\nAt 15.0% below base revenue and 3.5 points of margin compression, EBITDA is $2,526,300.00. Management's response remains unverified: Hiring pause and reduction of discretionary capital expenditure; not independently verified.\n\nITEMS NOT CLEARED\n— Confirm payoff amount for existing senior debt.\n— Validate the latest accounts-receivable aging against the general ledger.\n— Fuel surcharge recovery lagged diesel-cost changes by an average of 43 days in Q4 2025.\n— Obtain evidence for any sponsor support shown in the request.\n\nMATERIAL 2:\nONBOARDING ACTIVITY PROFILE\n\nObserved relationship as at 2026-04-15\n\nRECENT FLOWS FIRST\nObserved on | Payment rail | Amount | Counterparty description\n--- | --- | --- | ---\n2026-04-03 | incoming ACH | $279,500.00 | customer receipts batch\n2026-04-06 | domestic wire | $134,700.00 | equipment supplier\n2026-04-11 | international wire | $55,500.00 | overseas vendor\n\nEXPECTED PATTERN\nMonthly credits $3,826,666.67; monthly debits $3,482,266.67; domestic wires 39; international wires 6. Products requested: operating cash management, credit facility review, investment-policy reporting. Anticipated source: operating revenue and documented owner equity.\n\nWHO THE CLIENT IS\nBlue Harbor Logistics Holdings LLC was formed in Virginia on 2009-05-26 and operates in regional freight and warehousing. Tax identifier: XX-XXX0010. Principal location: 231 Commerce Way, Suite 203, Virginia.\n\nWHO CONTROLS IT\n— Marcus Vale holds 44.0% and acts as Chief Executive Officer.\n— Iris Chen holds 36.0% and acts as Chief Operating Officer.\n— Harbor Employee Trust holds 20.0% and acts as Employee trust.\n\nWHO MAY ACT\n— Marcus Vale: primary signer (verified).\n— Avery Chen: finance contact only (not verified).\n\nBALANCE-SHEET PROFILE\nCash / A/R / inventory: $2,035,000.00 / $8,420,000.00 / $640,000.00\nSenior debt: $11,700,000.00\nAnnual revenue / EBITDA: $45,920,000.00 / $4,010,000.00\n\nRISK PARAMETERS\nBusiness objective: fleet replacement and consolidation of equipment notes\nLiquidity minimum: $1,119,250.00\nRisk setting: moderate\nProhibited usage: cryptocurrency transfers, bearer instruments, undocumented third-party payments\nMonitoring note: Fuel surcharge recovery lagged diesel-cost changes by an average of 43 days in Q4 2025.\n\nSUPPORTING FILES\ncertificate of formation—present, 2009-05-26; ownership schedule—present, 2025-12-31; 2025 financial statements—present, 2025-12-31; secondary contact authority evidence—absent; current insurance certificate—absent\n\nQUERY:\nPrepare a credit committee brief assessing the collateral and diligence position for Blue Harbor Logistics Holdings LLC's proposed $9,500,000.00 delayed-draw term loan with a proposed close of 2030-09-30. Use only the supplied transaction desk snapshot and onboarding activity profile; label any result that cannot be established from these materials as Not Determinable.\n\nBegin by covering the named topics from the onboarding activity profile: ownership, control, authority, balance-sheet profile, and risk parameters. For each topic, identify the relevant facts and their as-of dates, and distinguish verified information from unverified or absent records.\n\nCalculate the variance between the fully drawn debt shown in the transaction desk snapshot and the sum of the senior debt shown in the onboarding activity profile plus the proposed delayed-draw term loan. Show both inputs and the resulting variance in U.S. dollars with exactly two decimal places, and state the units and basis for each input.\n\nCompare the base case EBITDA projections for FY2026, FY2027, and FY2028 with the break case EBITDA using the same period and unit. For each year, show the base case EBITDA, the break case EBITDA, and the absolute difference between them. Rank the three years by absolute difference from largest to smallest, and label each year's difference as Above, Below, or Roughly in Line relative to the break case EBITDA.\n\nAssess the preventive and detective controls relevant to the proposed delayed-draw loan, including the liquidity minimum, prohibited usage restrictions, and the monitoring note on fuel surcharge recovery lag. For each control, separate design from evidence that the control operated during the relevant period, and name the control owner where the materials support one.\n\nFlag each uncleared item and missing record as confirmed, unresolved, or dependent on missing evidence. Preserve the fuel surcharge recovery lag of 43 days in Q4 2025 as an unresolved inconsistency, and distinguish a confirmed gap from a potential gap that lacks required evidence.\n\nFor every uncleared item and missing record, state the corrective action, owner, deadline, and evidence required for closure, linking each action to the finding it resolves. Separate immediate containment from longer-term control remediation.\n\nIdentify which authorization evidence controls release of the proposed delayed-draw loan approval. Distinguish the verified primary signer, Marcus Vale, from the unverified finance contact, Avery Chen, and state which authorization evidence is required before the loan approval may be released. Do not imply approval while any authorization evidence remains pending or absent.\n\nReturn exactly three numbered findings, ordered by absolute variance from largest to smallest. Define all abbreviations on first use. Pair every recommendation with its controlling evidence and unresolved condition. Show every monetary difference in U.S. dollars with exactly two decimal places.",
