    "full_prompt": "MATERIAL 1:\nCREDIT REQUEST AND FINANCIAL INFORMATION\n\nBorrower: Northbridge Specialty Foods LLC\n\nREQUESTED FACILITY\nFacility | Amount | Pricing | Maturity\n--- | --- | --- | ---\nRevolving Credit | $6,500,000.00 | SOFR + 3.10% | 2030-06-30\nPurpose: seasonal working capital and refinancing of the existing revolver. Sponsor support proposed: $0.00.\n\nHISTORICAL FINANCIAL PERFORMANCE\nPeriod | Revenue | EBITDA | Cash interest | Capital expenditure\n--- | --- | --- | --- | ---\nFY2024 | $18,640,000.00 | $2,150,442.48 | $326,600.00 | $577,840.00\nFY2025 | $21,180,000.00 | $2,430,000.00 | $340,400.00 | $720,120.00\n\nThe supplied figures show revenue growth of 13.63%. At full draw, pro forma debt is $11,100,000.00, or 4.57x FY2025 EBITDA.\n\nBASE-CASE FORECAST\nPeriod | Revenue | EBITDA\n--- | --- | ---\nFY2026 | $22,874,400.00 | $2,600,100.00\nFY2027 | $24,357,000.00 | $2,818,800.00\nFY2028 | $25,839,600.00 | $3,037,500.00\n\nDOWNSIDE CASE\nRevenue is 12.0% below base and gross margin contracts by 2.0 points; estimated EBITDA is $1,749,600.00. Management's stated response is: Hiring pause and reduction of discretionary capital expenditure; not independently verified.\n\nCOLLATERAL SNAPSHOT\nCash | Eligible receivables | Inventory | Equipment value | Appraisal date\n--- | --- | --- | --- | ---\n$1,125,400.00 | $3,148,800.00 | $2,260,000.00 | $2,925,000.00 | 2025-09-30\n\nOPEN DILIGENCE ITEMS\n- Confirm payoff amount for existing senior debt.\n- Validate the latest accounts-receivable aging against the general ledger.\n- Customer concentration: the largest grocery chain represented 24.6% of 2025 revenue.\n- Obtain evidence for any sponsor support shown in the request.\n\nMATERIAL 2:\nOPERATIONS RECONCILIATION AND EXCEPTION REPORT\n\nEntity: Northbridge Specialty Foods LLC\nAs of: 2026-06-24\n\nCASH RECONCILIATION\nBank statement | Internal ledger | Deposit in transit | Adjusted break\n--- | --- | --- | ---\n$1,137,900.00 | $1,125,400.00 | $7,500.00 | $5,000.00\n\nUNRESOLVED CASH ITEMS\nReference | Amount | Age (days) | Owner\n--- | --- | --- | ---\nDEP-26-5100 | $7,500.00 | 1 | Treasury Operations\nFEE-26-6200 | $5,000.00 | 3 | Cash Control\n\nPOSITION SNAPSHOT\nAsset | Identifier | Quantity | Book value | Market value\n--- | --- | --- | --- | ---\nU.S. Treasury bill lot | TB-26-4100 | 1,000 | $985,000.00 | $989,500.00\nInvestment-grade bond lot | IG-26-7300 | 500 | $504,000.00 | $497,250.00\nOperating cash | CASH-26-8100 | 1 | $1,125,400.00 | $1,125,400.00\n\nTRADE ACTIVITY\nTrade ID | Trade date | Settlement | Side | Notional | Status | Counterparty\n--- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | ---\nTRD-26-101 | 2026-06-18 | 2026-06-20 | buy | $750,000.00 | settled | Dealer Alpha\nTRD-26-102 | 2026-06-20 | 2026-06-23 | sell | $320,000.00 | settled | Dealer Beta\n\nOPEN EXCEPTIONS\nException ID | Type | Amount | Opened | Owner | Support attached\n--- | --- | --- | --- | --- | ---\nEX-26-101 | cash break | $5,000.00 | 2026-06-23 | Cash Control | Yes\nEX-26-102 | missing confirmation | $320,000.00 | 2026-06-21 | Trade Support | Yes\n\nRECONCILIATION SIGN-OFF\nPrepared by R. Patel at 2026-06-25T14:20:00Z.\nReviewer: L. Grant; review timestamp: 2026-06-25T17:10:00Z.\n\nQUERY:\nPrepare a structure constraint brief for Northbridge Specialty Foods LLC that integrates the credit request and financial information with the operations reconciliation and exception report as of 2026-06-24. Write the brief for a credit committee reviewer: define abbreviations on first use, pair every constraint conclusion with its supporting source record, and keep the record and as-of dates separate.\n\nBegin with a one-sentence overall constraint status for the requested $6,500,000.00 revolving credit facility, then present the analysis in a table with columns `Scenario`, `EBITDA Input`, `Leverage Result`, `Supporting Record`, and `Constraint Status`.\n\nFor the quantitative verification, recalculate the stated 13.63% revenue growth from the FY2024 revenue of $18,640,000.00 and FY2025 revenue of $21,180,000.00, and independently verify the pro forma leverage multiple of 4.57x against the FY2025 EBITDA of $2,430,000.00 and the full-draw pro forma debt of $11,100,000.00. Show the inputs, formula, recalculated result, and any variance from the reported figure.\n\nCompare the leverage outcomes using the FY2026 base-case EBITDA of $2,600,100.00, the FY2027 base-case EBITDA of $2,818,800.00, the FY2028 base-case EBITDA of $3,037,500.00, and the downside-case estimated EBITDA of $1,749,600.00, all against the full-draw pro forma debt of $11,100,000.00. Rank the resulting leverage multiples by severity and label each scenario's constraint status.\n\nIdentify and cover the following unresolved items as structure constraints: the $5,000.00 cash break EX-26-101, the $320,000.00 missing confirmation EX-26-102, the unconfirmed payoff amount for existing senior debt, the unvalidated accounts-receivable aging against the general ledger, the 24.6% customer concentration represented by the largest grocery chain in 2025 revenue, and the unverified sponsor support shown as $0.00 in the request. For each item, state the affected population or exposure, the plausible impact, and the evidence limitation that prevents a clean conclusion.\n\nMark each unresolved item as open evidence and state which constraint conclusion it prevents. Do not infer a zero value or a clean reconciliation for any unmatched or missing record.\n\nCompare the base-case and downside-case EBITDA paths with management's stated response of a hiring pause and reduction of discretionary capital expenditure, noting the trade-off between forecast support and the fact that the management response is not independently verified.\n\nIdentify L. Grant's reviewer sign-off on the operations reconciliation as the required approval evidence, and state whether that sign-off authorizes closing the open exceptions or whether the exceptions remain open conditions.\n\nApply a hold or proceed condition to each structure constraint based on whether its supporting evidence is reconciled, approved, and free of unresolved exceptions. Where the evidence is incomplete, assign a hold and identify what is needed to resume.\n\nList the records reviewed and the documents to retain in the structure constraint workpaper, including the open diligence items from the credit request, the exception attachments for EX-26-101 and EX-26-102, and the reconciliation sign-off showing preparation by R. Patel and review by L. Grant.\n\nEnd with a `Next action:` line tied to the highest-priority unresolved evidence from the combined records.",
