    "full_prompt": "MATERIAL 1:\nEntity: CVS HEALTH CORPORATION\nCASH FLOW (USD, annual 10-K values)\nConcept (as reported) | FY end 2021-12-31 | FY end 2022-12-31 | FY end 2023-12-31 | FY end 2024-12-31 | FY end 2025-12-31\n--- | --- | --- | --- | --- | ---\nNetCashProvidedByUsedInOperatingActivities | 18,265,000,000 | 16,177,000,000 | 13,426,000,000 | 9,107,000,000 | 10,639,000,000\nNetCashProvidedByUsedInInvestingActivities | -5,261,000,000 | -5,047,000,000 | -20,889,000,000 | -7,613,000,000 | -5,871,000,000\nNetCashProvidedByUsedInFinancingActivities | -11,356,000,000 | -10,516,000,000 | 2,683,000,000 | -1,135,000,000 | -4,940,000,000\nPaymentsToAcquirePropertyPlantAndEquipment | 2,520,000,000 | 2,727,000,000 | 3,031,000,000 | 2,781,000,000 | 2,832,000,000\n\nMATERIAL 2:\nEntity: CVS HEALTH CORPORATION\nBALANCE SHEET (USD, annual 10-K values)\nConcept (as reported) | FY end 2021-12-31 | FY end 2022-12-31 | FY end 2023-12-31 | FY end 2024-12-31 | FY end 2025-12-31\n--- | --- | --- | --- | --- | ---\nAssets | 232,999,000,000 | 228,275,000,000 | 249,728,000,000 | 253,215,000,000 | 253,538,000,000\nLiabilities | 157,618,000,000 | 156,506,000,000 | 173,092,000,000 | 177,485,000,000 | 178,156,000,000\nStockholdersEquity | 75,075,000,000 | 71,469,000,000 | 76,461,000,000 | 75,560,000,000 | 75,214,000,000\nAssetsCurrent | 60,008,000,000 | 65,633,000,000 | 67,858,000,000 | 68,645,000,000 | 74,714,000,000\nLiabilitiesCurrent | 67,807,000,000 | 69,421,000,000 | 79,189,000,000 | 84,609,000,000 | 88,692,000,000\nCashAndCashEquivalentsAtCarryingValue | 9,408,000,000 | 12,945,000,000 | 8,196,000,000 | 8,586,000,000 | 8,453,000,000\nAccountsReceivableNetCurrent | 24,431,000,000 | 27,276,000,000 | 35,227,000,000 | 36,469,000,000 | 39,779,000,000\nInventoryNet | 17,760,000,000 | 19,090,000,000 | 18,025,000,000 | 18,107,000,000 | 19,246,000,000\nOtherLiabilitiesNoncurrent | 1,904,000,000 | 6,730,000,000 | 6,211,000,000 | 5,431,000,000 | 4,777,000,000\n\nQUERY:\nPrepare a capital allocation evidence brief for CVS HEALTH CORPORATION using only the supplied cash-flow and balance-sheet disclosures. The brief must integrate the two statements into one audit-ready analysis covering each aligned fiscal-year endpoint: 2021-12-31, 2022-12-31, 2023-12-31, 2024-12-31, and 2025-12-31.\n\nFor each fiscal year, calculate free cash flow as NetCashProvidedByUsedInOperatingActivities minus PaymentsToAcquirePropertyPlantAndEquipment, using the reported USD amounts exactly as disclosed and preserving signs and units. Do not round any source value before completing the calculation.\n\nIndependently recalculate the change in CashAndCashEquivalentsAtCarryingValue for each fiscal year by summing NetCashProvidedByUsedInOperatingActivities, NetCashProvidedByUsedInInvestingActivities, and NetCashProvidedByUsedInFinancingActivities from the cash-flow disclosure, then compare that recalculated change with the balance-sheet cash movement for the same fiscal year. Report any difference as a variance.\n\nUse only the two supplied disclosures. Do not add external market data, customary practice, legal assumptions, or any facts remembered from outside the packet. Where a needed input is not present in the supplied materials, preserve the missing status as `Not Determinable` rather than estimating it.\n\nFor every numeric input, calculated figure, recalculated figure, and variance, identify the supporting statement and concept beside the figure. Keep source labels next to each amount throughout the brief; end-only citations are insufficient.\n\nPreserve the exact reported concept names, fiscal-year endpoints, USD units, signs, and amounts from both disclosures. Do not relabel or round reported figures before completing the required calculations.\n\nPresent the results in a reconciliation table with columns `Fiscal Year`, `Source`, `Concept`, `Reported Amount`, `Recalculated Amount`, `Difference`, and `Status`. In the `Status` field use only `Ties Out`, `Variance`, or `Not Determinable`. Do not use the words `approved`, `closed`, or `reconciled` while any variance or missing input remains unresolved. Place narrative explanation outside the table.\n\nConclude the brief with a short evidence-integrated summary that connects the computed free cash flow, the recalculated cash movement, and any variances to the capital allocation picture shown by the two statements, without introducing information beyond the supplied disclosures.",
