    "full_prompt": "MATERIAL 1:\nEntity: DELTA AIR LINES, INC.\nCASH FLOW (USD, annual 10-K values)\nConcept (as reported) | FY end 2021-12-31 | FY end 2022-12-31 | FY end 2023-12-31 | FY end 2024-12-31 | FY end 2025-12-31\n--- | --- | --- | --- | --- | ---\nNetCashProvidedByUsedInOperatingActivities | 3,264,000,000 | 6,363,000,000 | 6,464,000,000 | 8,025,000,000 | 8,342,000,000\nNetCashProvidedByUsedInInvestingActivities | -898,000,000 | -6,924,000,000 | -3,148,000,000 | -3,739,000,000 | -4,186,000,000\nNetCashProvidedByUsedInFinancingActivities | -3,852,000,000 | -4,535,000,000 | -3,394,000,000 | -4,260,000,000 | -3,076,000,000\n\nMATERIAL 2:\nEntity: DELTA AIR LINES, INC.\nBALANCE SHEET (USD, annual 10-K values)\nConcept (as reported) | FY end 2021-12-31 | FY end 2022-12-31 | FY end 2023-12-31 | FY end 2024-12-31 | FY end 2025-12-31\n--- | --- | --- | --- | --- | ---\nAssets | 72,459,000,000 | 72,288,000,000 | 73,644,000,000 | 75,372,000,000 | 81,317,000,000\nLiabilitiesCurrent | 20,966,000,000 | 25,940,000,000 | 26,418,000,000 | 26,670,000,000 | 27,624,000,000\nStockholdersEquity | 3,887,000,000 | 6,582,000,000 | 11,105,000,000 | 15,293,000,000 | 20,853,000,000\nAssetsCurrent | 15,940,000,000 | 13,011,000,000 | 10,269,000,000 | 9,844,000,000 | 10,968,000,000\nCashAndCashEquivalentsAtCarryingValue | 7,933,000,000 | 3,266,000,000 | 2,741,000,000 | 3,069,000,000 | 4,310,000,000\nAirlineRelatedInventoryNet | 1,098,000,000 | 1,424,000,000 | 1,314,000,000 | 1,428,000,000 | 1,601,000,000\nLongTermDebtNoncurrent | 23,582,000,000 | 19,326,000,000 | 15,985,000,000 | 13,546,000,000 | 11,936,000,000\nLongTermDebt | 25,084,000,000 | 21,381,000,000 | 18,610,000,000 | 15,347,000,000 | 13,308,000,000\nLiabilitiesNoncurrent | 47,606,000,000 | 39,766,000,000 | 36,121,000,000 | 33,409,000,000 | 32,840,000,000\n\nQUERY:\nPrepare a downside case evidence brief for DELTA AIR LINES, INC. that integrates the supplied annual 10-K balance sheet and cash flow disclosures for the aligned fiscal years ending 2021-12-31 through 2025-12-31. Use only the two supplied materials and preserve every source figure, concept label, sign, unit, and FY-end date exactly as reported, including the negative investing and financing cash flow amounts. For each aligned FY end, apply the same period consistently across both statements and flag any period where the balance sheet and cash flow columns cannot be matched to the same FY end. Build the brief around the reported concepts only: from the balance sheet use Assets, LiabilitiesCurrent, StockholdersEquity, AssetsCurrent, CashAndCashEquivalentsAtCarryingValue, AirlineRelatedInventoryNet, LongTermDebtNoncurrent, LongTermDebt, and LiabilitiesNoncurrent; from the cash flow statement use NetCashProvidedByUsedInOperatingActivities, NetCashProvidedByUsedInInvestingActivities, and NetCashProvidedByUsedInFinancingActivities. For each aligned FY end, compute the downside-case indicators required to assess liquidity and leverage, stating the formula for each indicator and showing all inputs with their source labels. Independently verify the reported figures against each other where the two statements should tie out, show any unexplained variance, and state whether each check ties out. Map every downside-case finding back to the exact balance sheet or cash flow concept and FY-end figure used, keeping the source label beside each input and result. Use only the labels `Supported`, `Partially Supported`, and `Not Determinable` for each finding; do not use `Pass`, `Fail`, `Approved`, or `Rejected`. Where a needed input is absent from the supplied materials, preserve the missing status as `Not Determinable` rather than estimating or importing external facts. Close the brief with a one-sentence readiness gate stating which downside-case evidence remains unresolved and which additional record would be required to change the gate.",
