    "full_prompt": "MATERIAL 1:\nTRANSACTION DESK SNAPSHOT\n\nBlue Harbor Logistics Holdings LLC | proposed close: 2030-09-30\n\nSTRUCTURE AT A GLANCE\nDELAYED-DRAW TERM LOAN / $9,500,000.00 / SOFR + 3.40%\nPurpose — fleet replacement and consolidation of equipment notes\nSponsor amount identified — $2,250,000.00\n\nLEVERAGE READOUT\nLatest revenue change: -2.92%\nFully drawn debt: $21,200,000.00\nPro forma leverage: 5.29x\n\nTWO-YEAR ACTUALS\nYear | Turnover | EBITDA | Interest paid | Capex\n--- | --- | --- | --- | ---\nFY2024 | $47,300,000.00 | $3,548,672.57 | $830,700.00 | $2,033,900.00\nFY2025 | $45,920,000.00 | $4,010,000.00 | $865,800.00 | $2,112,320.00\n\nASSET COVERAGE NOTES\n• $2,035,000.00 cash\n• $6,904,400.00 preliminary eligible receivables\n• $640,000.00 inventory at book\n• $5,415,000.00 equipment value (2025-12-30)\n\nBASE PROJECTION\nFY2026: $49,593,600.00 revenue / $4,290,700.00 EBITDA | FY2027: $52,808,000.00 revenue / $4,651,600.00 EBITDA | FY2028: $56,022,400.00 revenue / $5,012,500.00 EBITDA\n\nBREAK CASE\nAt 15.0% below base revenue and 3.5 points of margin compression, EBITDA is $2,526,300.00. Management's response remains unverified: Hiring pause and reduction of discretionary capital expenditure; not independently verified.\n\nITEMS NOT CLEARED\n— Confirm payoff amount for existing senior debt.\n— Validate the latest accounts-receivable aging against the general ledger.\n— Fuel surcharge recovery lagged diesel-cost changes by an average of 43 days in Q4 2025.\n— Obtain evidence for any sponsor support shown in the request.\n\nMATERIAL 2:\nONBOARDING ACTIVITY PROFILE\n\nObserved relationship as at 2026-04-15\n\nRECENT FLOWS FIRST\nObserved on | Payment rail | Amount | Counterparty description\n--- | --- | --- | ---\n2026-04-03 | incoming ACH | $279,500.00 | customer receipts batch\n2026-04-06 | domestic wire | $134,700.00 | equipment supplier\n2026-04-11 | international wire | $55,500.00 | overseas vendor\n\nEXPECTED PATTERN\nMonthly credits $3,826,666.67; monthly debits $3,482,266.67; domestic wires 39; international wires 6. Products requested: operating cash management, credit facility review, investment-policy reporting. Anticipated source: operating revenue and documented owner equity.\n\nWHO THE CLIENT IS\nBlue Harbor Logistics Holdings LLC was formed in Virginia on 2009-05-26 and operates in regional freight and warehousing. Tax identifier: XX-XXX0010. Principal location: 231 Commerce Way, Suite 203, Virginia.\n\nWHO CONTROLS IT\n— Marcus Vale holds 44.0% and acts as Chief Executive Officer.\n— Iris Chen holds 36.0% and acts as Chief Operating Officer.\n— Harbor Employee Trust holds 20.0% and acts as Employee trust.\n\nWHO MAY ACT\n— Marcus Vale: primary signer (verified).\n— Avery Chen: finance contact only (not verified).\n\nBALANCE-SHEET PROFILE\nCash / A/R / inventory: $2,035,000.00 / $8,420,000.00 / $640,000.00\nSenior debt: $11,700,000.00\nAnnual revenue / EBITDA: $45,920,000.00 / $4,010,000.00\n\nRISK PARAMETERS\nBusiness objective: fleet replacement and consolidation of equipment notes\nLiquidity minimum: $1,119,250.00\nRisk setting: moderate\nProhibited usage: cryptocurrency transfers, bearer instruments, undocumented third-party payments\nMonitoring note: Fuel surcharge recovery lagged diesel-cost changes by an average of 43 days in Q4 2025.\n\nSUPPORTING FILES\ncertificate of formation—present, 2009-05-26; ownership schedule—present, 2025-12-31; 2025 financial statements—present, 2025-12-31; secondary contact authority evidence—absent; current insurance certificate—absent\n\nQUERY:\nPrepare the Blue Harbor Logistics Holdings LLC proposed delayed-draw term loan collateral and diligence assessment brief as an evidence-integrated revision using only the TRANSACTION DESK SNAPSHOT and the ONBOARDING ACTIVITY PROFILE. Open with a one-sentence collateral coverage status conclusion, then present exactly four numbered sections in this order: (1) Collateral and Diligence Status, (2) Leverage and Coverage Calculations, (3) Risk and Impact Assessment, and (4) Open Evidence and Remediation. Use the exact status labels `Cleared`, `Open`, and `Not Determinable` for every collateral and diligence item, and do not use `approved` or `final` anywhere in the brief. Show every monetary amount to two decimal places and every ratio to two decimal places. Add a `Source` column to every table and place a source label beside every numeric input, status determination, and risk conclusion, citing either the TRANSACTION DESK SNAPSHOT or the ONBOARDING ACTIVITY PROFILE and the specific figure or clause used. Preserve the exact entity name, proposed close date of 2030-09-30, loan amount of $9,500,000.00, margin of SOFR + 3.40%, ownership percentages, signer names, record dates, and all source figures and thresholds exactly as they appear in the two records, without rounding or relabeling. In Section 1, compare the FY2024 and FY2025 actual turnover and EBITDA figures against the FY2026 base projection on the same annual basis, then rank the three periods by EBITDA from highest to lowest. For each collateral and diligence item, connect the active evidence from the transaction desk snapshot or onboarding profile, the applicable risk parameter or transaction term, and the resulting `Cleared`, `Open`, or `Not Determinable` status. Identify which named individual or entity in the onboarding profile has the authority to approve the proposed delayed-draw term loan on behalf of Blue Harbor Logistics Holdings LLC, and state whether that authority is verified or remains unverified. In Section 2, calculate the proposed fully drawn total debt as the existing senior debt of $11,700,000.00 from the onboarding profile plus the proposed delayed-draw term loan amount of $9,500,000.00 from the transaction desk snapshot, and separately calculate the pro forma leverage multiple using that total and the FY2025 EBITDA of $4,010,000.00. In Section 3, for the break case EBITDA of $2,526,300.00, the unverified management response of a hiring pause and reduction of discretionary capital expenditure, the fuel surcharge recovery lag of 43 days in Q4 2025, and the absent current insurance certificate, describe the affected population, the plausible financial or operational exposure, and the evidence limitation that prevents quantification. In Section 4, list every missing or unverified item from the transaction desk `ITEMS NOT CLEARED` list and the onboarding `SUPPORTING FILES` list under a single `Open Evidence` subsection, and state which calculation or status each missing item prevents. For each `Open` item, state the corrective action or evidence to obtain, the owner from the onboarding profile, and the condition that must be satisfied before the item can move to `Cleared`. Close with a single `Next action:` line identifying the most urgent unresolved diligence item from the two records.",
