    "full_prompt": "MATERIAL 1:\nCREDIT REQUEST AND FINANCIAL INFORMATION\n\nBorrower: Northbridge Specialty Foods LLC\n\nREQUESTED FACILITY\nFacility | Amount | Pricing | Maturity\n--- | --- | --- | ---\nRevolving Credit | $6,500,000.00 | SOFR + 3.10% | 2030-06-30\nPurpose: seasonal working capital and refinancing of the existing revolver. Sponsor support proposed: $0.00.\n\nHISTORICAL FINANCIAL PERFORMANCE\nPeriod | Revenue | EBITDA | Cash interest | Capital expenditure\n--- | --- | --- | --- | ---\nFY2024 | $18,640,000.00 | $2,150,442.48 | $326,600.00 | $577,840.00\nFY2025 | $21,180,000.00 | $2,430,000.00 | $340,400.00 | $720,120.00\n\nThe supplied figures show revenue growth of 13.63%. At full draw, pro forma debt is $11,100,000.00, or 4.57x FY2025 EBITDA.\n\nBASE-CASE FORECAST\nPeriod | Revenue | EBITDA\n--- | --- | ---\nFY2026 | $22,874,400.00 | $2,600,100.00\nFY2027 | $24,357,000.00 | $2,818,800.00\nFY2028 | $25,839,600.00 | $3,037,500.00\n\nDOWNSIDE CASE\nRevenue is 12.0% below base and gross margin contracts by 2.0 points; estimated EBITDA is $1,749,600.00. Management's stated response is: Hiring pause and reduction of discretionary capital expenditure; not independently verified.\n\nCOLLATERAL SNAPSHOT\nCash | Eligible receivables | Inventory | Equipment value | Appraisal date\n--- | --- | --- | --- | ---\n$1,125,400.00 | $3,148,800.00 | $2,260,000.00 | $2,925,000.00 | 2025-09-30\n\nOPEN DILIGENCE ITEMS\n- Confirm payoff amount for existing senior debt.\n- Validate the latest accounts-receivable aging against the general ledger.\n- Customer concentration: the largest grocery chain represented 24.6% of 2025 revenue.\n- Obtain evidence for any sponsor support shown in the request.\n\nMATERIAL 2:\nCLIENT INTAKE AND FINANCIAL PROFILE\n\nRecord date: 2026-01-15\n\nENTITY PROFILE\nLegal name | Jurisdiction | Formation date | Industry | Tax ID | Operating address\n--- | --- | --- | --- | --- | ---\nNorthbridge Specialty Foods LLC | Delaware | 2014-03-18 | specialty food distribution | XX-XXX0007 | 120 Commerce Way, Suite 200, Delaware\n\nOWNERSHIP AND CONTROL\nName | Ownership | Role\n--- | --- | ---\nElena Marlow | 62.0% | Managing Member\nJonah Reeves | 38.0% | Operations Member\n\nAUTHORIZED CONTACTS\nName | Authority | Verified\n--- | --- | ---\nElena Marlow | primary signer | Yes\nJordan Blake | finance contact only | No\n\nREQUESTED RELATIONSHIP\nRequested services: operating cash management, credit facility review, investment-policy reporting.\nExpected monthly inflows | Expected monthly outflows | Domestic wires/month | International wires/month\n--- | --- | --- | ---\n$1,765,000.00 | $1,606,150.00 | 18 | 0\nSource of funds: operating revenue and documented owner equity\n\nFINANCIAL PROFILE\nCash | Accounts receivable | Inventory | Senior debt | Annual revenue | Annual EBITDA\n--- | --- | --- | --- | --- | ---\n$1,125,400.00 | $3,840,000.00 | $2,260,000.00 | $4,600,000.00 | $21,180,000.00 | $2,430,000.00\n\nOBJECTIVES AND CONSTRAINTS\nPrimary objective: seasonal working capital and refinancing of the existing revolver.\nRequested liquidity floor: $618,970.00. Risk tolerance: moderate.\nRestricted activities: cryptocurrency transfers, bearer instruments, undocumented third-party payments.\nRisk observation: Customer concentration: the largest grocery chain represented 24.6% of 2025 revenue.\n\nDOCUMENT CHECKLIST\nDocument | Received | As of\n--- | --- | ---\ncertificate of formation | Yes | 2014-03-18\nownership schedule | Yes | 2025-12-31\n2025 financial statements | Yes | 2025-12-31\nsecondary contact authority evidence | No | —\ncurrent insurance certificate | Yes | 2026-01-31\n\nRECENT ACTIVITY SAMPLE\nDate | Type | Amount | Counterparty\n--- | --- | --- | ---\n2026-01-03 | incoming ACH | $184,250.00 | customer receipts batch\n2026-01-06 | domestic wire | $92,400.00 | equipment supplier\n2026-01-11 | international wire | $0.00 | None\n\nQUERY:\nPrepare an evidence-integrated collateral and diligence assessment brief for Northbridge Specialty Foods LLC's proposed $6,500,000.00 revolving credit facility for review by the credit committee. Write the brief for a credit committee audience: define all abbreviations on first use, pair every recommendation with its controlling evidence, and clearly distinguish confirmed facts from unverified, pending, or missing items. Use only the two supplied records — the credit request and financial information and the client intake and financial profile — and do not import any external market data, customary lending practices, legal assumptions, or facts not present in the packet. Where a needed input is absent, label the result as Not Determinable rather than estimating it.\n\nBegin the brief with a one-sentence Proceed, Hold, or Escalate decision, and end with a Next action line tied to the highest-priority unresolved diligence item.\n\nStructure the brief as follows:\n\n1. Evidence reconciliation. Reconcile the financial profile figures in the client intake record against the corresponding figures in the credit request. Match the cash, inventory, annual revenue, and annual EBITDA fields across the two records, calculate each difference, and retain any non-zero item as Unresolved. Separately compare the accounts receivable figures: the credit request collateral snapshot shows eligible receivables of $3,148,800.00, while the intake financial profile shows accounts receivable of $3,840,000.00. Do not mark the records reconciled where any mismatch remains.\n\n2. Independent recalculation. Independently recalculate the reported revenue growth of 13.63% using the FY2024 revenue of $18,640,000.00 and the FY2025 revenue of $21,180,000.00. Show the formula, the inputs, the recalculated result, and the variance from the reported 13.63%, and state whether the reported figure ties out. Preserve all source figures, dates, thresholds, and entity names exactly as written, including the SOFR + 3.10% pricing, the 2030-06-30 maturity, the 2025-09-30 appraisal date, the 24.6% customer concentration, and the 2026-01-15 record date. Do not round source values before completing any comparison.\n\n3. Risk and impact coverage. For each finding below, state the affected population, exposure, plausible impact, and evidence limitation, separating quantified exposure from qualitative consequences that cannot be measured from the packet:\n   a. Downside-case risk: revenue 12.0% below base and gross margin contracting by 2.0 points, with estimated EBITDA of $1,749,600.00.\n   b. Customer concentration risk: the largest grocery chain represented 24.6% of 2025 revenue.\n   c. Unverified management response risk: the stated hiring pause and reduction of discretionary capital expenditure is not independently verified.\n\n4. Scenario comparison. Compare the base-case forecast and the downside case on revenue, EBITDA, and the resulting leverage or coverage implications. State the benefit, limitation, and decision implication of relying on each scenario.\n\n5. Deficiency classification. Identify each supplied deficiency as confirmed, unresolved, or dependent on missing evidence, distinguishing:\n   a. The unconfirmed payoff amount for existing senior debt.\n   b. The unvalidated latest accounts-receivable aging against the general ledger.\n   c. The unverified management response.\n   d. The missing evidence for any sponsor support shown in the request, noting that the credit request states sponsor support proposed is $0.00.\n\n6. Remediation plan. For every open diligence item, state the corrective action, owner, deadline, and evidence required for closure, linking each action to the specific finding it resolves.\n\n7. Evidence-rule-action chain. For each decision, show the active evidence, the applicable rule or task standard, and the resulting action in one connected chain, so that the collateral assessment, diligence findings, and recommendation are not presented as disconnected fragments. Connect the calculated threshold results and unresolved mismatches to the Proceed, Hold, or Escalate decision.\n\nClose with a Next action line tied to the highest-priority unresolved diligence item.",
