    "full_prompt": "MATERIAL 1:\n[Continues under: Prohibitions:11]\n\nInclusion or exclusion of performance results or time periods in manners that were not fair and balanced.22 The staff observed advertisements that included or excluded certain performance results or presented performance time periods in manners that were not fair and balanced. For example:\n\n• Advertisements that did not disclose the time period or did not disclose whether the returns were calculated for the same time period as additional performance information included in the same advertisement.\n\n• Advertisements that included or excluded certain performance results in manners that were not fair and balanced, such as advertisements that included the performance of only realized investment information in the total net return figure and excluded unrealized investments.\n\nAdvertisements that were otherwise materially misleading.23 The staff observed advertisements that appeared to otherwise be materially misleading, such as presenting disclosures in an unreadable font on websites or in videos.\n\nIV. Conclusion\n\nIn sharing these staff observations, the Division encourages advisers to reflect upon their own practices, policies, and procedures and to implement any appropriate modifications to their training, supervisory, oversight, and compliance programs.\n\n22 See Advisers Act Rule 206(4)-1(a)(6).\n\n23 See Advisers Act Rule 206(4)-1(a)(7).\n\nThis Risk Alert is intended to highlight for firms risks and issues that Division staff has identified.\n\n[Continues under: IV. Conclusion]\n\nIn addition, this Risk Alert describes risks that firms may consider to (1) assess their supervisory, compliance, and/or other risk management systems related to these risks, and (2) make any changes, as may be appropriate, to address or strengthen such systems. Other risks besides those described in this Risk Alert may be appropriate to consider, and some issues discussed in this Risk Alert may not be relevant to a particular firm’s business. The adequacy of supervisory, compliance and other risk management systems can be determined only with reference to the profile of each specific firm and other facts and circumstances.\n\nQUERY:\nPrepare a compliance review evidence specification brief covering performance periods and presentation balance in adviser advertisements, using only the supplied SEC Division of Examinations Risk Alert. The brief must specify the evidence needed to review whether advertisements comply with the fair-and-balanced and materially misleading boundaries described in the Risk Alert, without treating any staff observation as a current or guaranteed performance claim.\n\nStructure the brief as a table with the following columns: `Review Area`, `Observed Deficiency`, `Classification`, `Evidence Required`, `Remediation Action`, `Owner`, and `Deadline`.\n\nCover the following review areas as distinct rows: (1) failure to disclose the time period for performance results; (2) failure to disclose whether returns were calculated for the same time period as additional performance information in the same advertisement; (3) inclusion or exclusion of certain performance results in a manner that was not fair and balanced, such as including only realized investment information in a total net return figure while excluding unrealized investments; and (4) otherwise materially misleading presentation, such as unreadable font on websites or in videos.\n\nFor each review area, preserve the Risk Alert's exact deficiency wording, time-period references, and rule citations wherever they control the evidence requirement. Classify each observed deficiency using only one of the following status labels: `Confirmed Gap`, `Unresolved Inconsistency`, or `Missing Evidence`. If the Risk Alert does not supply enough information to support a classification, use `Not Determinable` instead.\n\nFor every identified deficiency, state the corrective action, owner, deadline, and evidence required for closure, linking each action to the specific staff observation it resolves. Include the exact label `Evidence Required:` exactly once per review area, followed by the specific documents, records, or information a compliance reviewer would need to test that review area.\n\nAddress the compliance program elements the Risk Alert identifies for modification, including training, supervisory, oversight, and compliance programs. For each element, specify the control evidence needed to demonstrate that the element has been modified to address the observed performance-period and presentation-balance deficiencies.\n\nDo not add any outside facts, market data, customary practice, legal assumptions, or information not present in the supplied Risk Alert. If a required evidence item, owner, or deadline cannot be established from the material, preserve that missing status rather than estimating it.",
