    "full_prompt": "MATERIAL 1:\nEntity: CATERPILLAR INC\nINCOME STATEMENT (USD, annual 10-K values)\nConcept (as reported) | FY end 2021-12-31 | FY end 2022-12-31 | FY end 2023-12-31 | FY end 2024-12-31 | FY end 2025-12-31\n--- | --- | --- | --- | --- | ---\nRevenues | 50,971,000,000 | 59,427,000,000 | 67,060,000,000 | 64,809,000,000 | 67,589,000,000\nCostOfRevenue | 35,513,000,000 | 41,350,000,000 | 42,767,000,000 | 40,199,000,000 | 44,752,000,000\nCostOfGoodsAndServicesSold | — | 413,000,000 | 160,000,000 | 33,000,000 | 49,000,000\nOperatingIncomeLoss | 6,878,000,000 | 7,904,000,000 | 12,966,000,000 | 13,072,000,000 | 11,151,000,000\nIncomeTaxExpenseBenefit | 1,742,000,000 | 2,067,000,000 | 2,781,000,000 | 2,629,000,000 | 2,768,000,000\nResearchAndDevelopmentExpense | 1,686,000,000 | 1,814,000,000 | 2,108,000,000 | 2,107,000,000 | 2,148,000,000\nEarningsPerShareBasic (USD/shares) | 11.93 | 12.72 | 20.24 | 22.17 | 18.9\n\nMATERIAL 2:\nEntity: CATERPILLAR INC\nBALANCE SHEET (USD, annual 10-K values)\nConcept (as reported) | FY end 2021-12-31 | FY end 2022-12-31 | FY end 2023-12-31 | FY end 2024-12-31 | FY end 2025-12-31\n--- | --- | --- | --- | --- | ---\nAssets | 82,793,000,000 | 81,943,000,000 | 87,476,000,000 | 87,764,000,000 | 98,585,000,000\nLiabilities | 66,277,000,000 | 66,052,000,000 | 67,973,000,000 | 68,270,000,000 | 77,267,000,000\nStockholdersEquityOther | -35,000,000 | -44,000,000 | -4,000,000 | 2,000,000 | 5,000,000\nAssetsCurrent | 43,455,000,000 | 43,785,000,000 | 46,949,000,000 | 45,682,000,000 | 52,485,000,000\nLiabilitiesCurrent | 29,847,000,000 | 31,531,000,000 | 34,728,000,000 | 32,272,000,000 | 36,558,000,000\nCashAndCashEquivalentsAtCarryingValue | 9,254,000,000 | 7,004,000,000 | 6,978,000,000 | 6,889,000,000 | 9,980,000,000\nAccountsReceivableNetCurrent | 8,477,000,000 | 8,856,000,000 | 9,310,000,000 | 9,282,000,000 | 10,920,000,000\nInventoryNet | 14,038,000,000 | 16,270,000,000 | 16,565,000,000 | 16,827,000,000 | 18,135,000,000\nLongTermDebtNoncurrent | 26,033,000,000 | 25,714,000,000 | 24,472,000,000 | 27,351,000,000 | 30,696,000,000\n\nMATERIAL 3:\nEntity: CATERPILLAR INC\nCASH FLOW (USD, annual 10-K values)\nConcept (as reported) | FY end 2021-12-31 | FY end 2022-12-31 | FY end 2023-12-31 | FY end 2024-12-31 | FY end 2025-12-31\n--- | --- | --- | --- | --- | ---\nNetCashProvidedByUsedInOperatingActivities | 7,198,000,000 | 7,766,000,000 | 12,885,000,000 | 12,035,000,000 | 11,739,000,000\nNetCashProvidedByUsedInInvestingActivities | -3,084,000,000 | -2,541,000,000 | -5,871,000,000 | -2,453,000,000 | -4,707,000,000\nNetCashProvidedByUsedInFinancingActivities | -4,188,000,000 | -7,281,000,000 | -6,932,000,000 | -9,565,000,000 | -3,899,000,000\nPaymentsToAcquirePropertyPlantAndEquipment | 1,093,000,000 | 1,296,000,000 | 1,597,000,000 | 1,988,000,000 | 2,821,000,000\n\nQUERY:\nPrepare a profitability reporting consistency brief for Caterpillar Inc.'s annual 10-K statements covering the fiscal years ended 2021-12-31 through 2025-12-31, using only the supplied income statement, balance sheet, and cash flow materials. Preserve the exact concept labels, USD units, fiscal-year endpoints, and as-reported values from those materials wherever they are used as inputs or compared.\n\nIndependently recalculate the following metrics for each fiscal year and show the recalculated result, the reported or implied value, the difference in USD, and whether the metric ties out:\n1. Operating margin, calculated as OperatingIncomeLoss divided by Revenues.\n2. Operating cash flow to operating income, calculated as NetCashProvidedByUsedInOperatingActivities divided by OperatingIncomeLoss.\n3. Current ratio, calculated as AssetsCurrent divided by LiabilitiesCurrent.\n\nFor each recalculated metric, use only the labels 'Ties Out', 'Variance', and 'Not Determinable' for its consistency status. Show every percentage with exactly two decimal places and every monetary difference in USD. Where a required input is absent from the supplied materials, label the result 'Not Determinable' rather than estimating it.\n\nMap every recalculated metric, variance, and cross-statement check to the exact source concept and fiscal-year value used, keeping source labels beside each input and result.\n\nPresent the recalculation results in a table with columns 'Fiscal Year', 'Metric', 'Source Inputs', 'Recalculated Value', 'Reported/Implied Value', 'Difference (USD)', and 'Status'.\n\nApply the FY2021-12-31 through FY2025-12-31 fiscal-year endpoints consistently across all income statement, balance sheet, and cash flow inputs, and flag any period misalignment in the cross-statement analysis.\n\nInclude the exact label 'Cross-Statement Check:' once before the integrated analysis. In that section, compare the operating income trend from the income statement with the operating cash flow trend from the cash flow statement for each fiscal year, and identify any year in which the two trends diverge in direction or magnitude, citing the specific source values used.\n\nEnd with exactly three numbered findings, ordered by absolute variance from largest to smallest, where each finding identifies the metric, fiscal year, source inputs, recalculated value, reported or implied value, difference in USD, and consistency status. Do not supply the final calculated results in this instruction; the brief must derive them from the supplied materials.",
