    "full_prompt": "MATERIAL 1:\nOPERATIONS BREAK CASE RECORD\n\nCase entity: Blue Harbor Logistics Holdings LLC\nPosition date: 2026-06-27\n\nOPEN CASES\nBreak reference | Finding | Amount at risk | Open since | Desk | Backup\n--- | --- | --- | --- | --- | ---\nEX-26-401 | cash break | $20,000.00 | 2026-06-26 | Cash Control | received\nEX-26-402 | missing confirmation | $560,000.00 | 2026-06-24 | Trade Support | not received\n\nRECONCILIATION NARRATIVE\nExternal cash of $2,085,000.00 exceeds recorded cash of $2,035,000.00. A $30,000.00 timing item is documented, leaving $20,000.00 unresolved.\n\nDIFFERENCE OWNERSHIP\nDEP-26-5103 → Treasury Operations | $30,000.00 | age 4 days\nFEE-26-6203 → Cash Control | $20,000.00 | age 9 days\n\nTRADES CONNECTED TO THE PERIOD\n• TRD-26-401: buy $1,125,000.00; 2026-06-21 trade / 2026-06-23 settlement; settled; Dealer Alpha\n• TRD-26-402: sell $560,000.00; 2026-06-23 trade / 2026-06-26 settlement; pending confirmation; Dealer Beta\n\nBOOK-TO-MARK INVENTORY\nInstrument | Lot | Position size | Accounting value | Market mark\n--- | --- | --- | --- | ---\nU.S. Treasury bill lot | TB-26-4103 | 1,750 | $1,667,500.00 | $1,676,500.00\nInvestment-grade bond lot | IG-26-7303 | 800 | $810,000.00 | $792,750.00\nOperating cash | CASH-26-8103 | 1 | $2,035,000.00 | $2,035,000.00\n\nAPPROVAL STATE\nOperations record completed by D. Foster at 2026-06-28T14:20:00Z. Reviewer: not assigned. Approval time: pending.\n\nMATERIAL 2:\nONBOARDING ACTIVITY PROFILE\n\nObserved relationship as at 2026-04-15\n\nRECENT FLOWS FIRST\nObserved on | Payment rail | Amount | Counterparty description\n--- | --- | --- | ---\n2026-04-03 | incoming ACH | $279,500.00 | customer receipts batch\n2026-04-06 | domestic wire | $134,700.00 | equipment supplier\n2026-04-11 | international wire | $55,500.00 | overseas vendor\n\nEXPECTED PATTERN\nMonthly credits $3,826,666.67; monthly debits $3,482,266.67; domestic wires 39; international wires 6. Products requested: operating cash management, credit facility review, investment-policy reporting. Anticipated source: operating revenue and documented owner equity.\n\nWHO THE CLIENT IS\nBlue Harbor Logistics Holdings LLC was formed in Virginia on 2009-05-26 and operates in regional freight and warehousing. Tax identifier: XX-XXX0010. Principal location: 231 Commerce Way, Suite 203, Virginia.\n\nWHO CONTROLS IT\n— Marcus Vale holds 44.0% and acts as Chief Executive Officer.\n— Iris Chen holds 36.0% and acts as Chief Operating Officer.\n— Harbor Employee Trust holds 20.0% and acts as Employee trust.\n\nWHO MAY ACT\n— Marcus Vale: primary signer (verified).\n— Avery Chen: finance contact only (not verified).\n\nBALANCE-SHEET PROFILE\nCash / A/R / inventory: $2,035,000.00 / $8,420,000.00 / $640,000.00\nSenior debt: $11,700,000.00\nAnnual revenue / EBITDA: $45,920,000.00 / $4,010,000.00\n\nRISK PARAMETERS\nBusiness objective: fleet replacement and consolidation of equipment notes\nLiquidity minimum: $1,119,250.00\nRisk setting: moderate\nProhibited usage: cryptocurrency transfers, bearer instruments, undocumented third-party payments\nMonitoring note: Fuel surcharge recovery lagged diesel-cost changes by an average of 43 days in Q4 2025.\n\nSUPPORTING FILES\ncertificate of formation—present, 2009-05-26; ownership schedule—present, 2025-12-31; 2025 financial statements—present, 2025-12-31; secondary contact authority evidence—absent; current insurance certificate—absent\n\nQUERY:\nPrepare an exception handling evidence brief for Blue Harbor Logistics Holdings LLC for internal operations and compliance review. Use only the OPERATIONS BREAK CASE RECORD and the ONBOARDING ACTIVITY PROFILE as evidence sources, and keep the record and as-of dates separate throughout.\n\nStructure the brief with level-2 headings in this order: `Records Reviewed`, `Exception and Risk Coverage`, `Reconciliation`, `Approval and Authorization`, and `Open Items`.\n\nUnder `Records Reviewed`, list the evidence reviewed and the documents to retain in the brief workpaper. Identify for each open exception the supporting record and any missing document needed to close the file: for EX-26-401, state the backup status `received`; for EX-26-402, state the backup status `not received`; and from the onboarding profile, list the supporting file statuses, including `secondary contact authority evidence—absent` and `current insurance certificate—absent`.\n\nUnder `Exception and Risk Coverage`, for each open exception and the unresolved reconciliation difference, state the affected exposure, the specific risk it permits, and the evidence limitation that prevents measuring the full impact. Address the $560,000.00 missing confirmation exposure on TRD-26-402, the $20,000.00 unresolved cash break on EX-26-401, and the monitoring note that fuel surcharge recovery lagged diesel-cost changes by an average of 43 days in Q4 2025. Cover the entity identification, control ownership, authorized actors, balance-sheet profile, and risk parameters from the onboarding profile, and connect each covered item to the exception handling analysis where it affects authority, exposure, or missing documentation.\n\nUnder `Reconciliation`, reconcile the recorded cash balance of $2,035,000.00 from the operations record against the cash figure of $2,035,000.00 in the onboarding balance-sheet profile. Separately match the external cash of $2,085,000.00, the $30,000.00 timing item, and the $20,000.00 unresolved difference, and retain any non-zero or unmatched item as `Unresolved`. Independently verify the reported recorded cash of $2,035,000.00 by recalculating it from the external cash of $2,085,000.00 less the $30,000.00 timing item and the $20,000.00 unresolved difference, and state whether the reported figure ties out.\n\nUnder `Approval and Authorization`, state the required approval and authorization status for the operations record. Distinguish the completed entry by D. Foster at 2026-06-28T14:20:00Z from the unassigned reviewer and the pending approval time, and identify which actor from the onboarding profile holds verified signing authority to act on any exception disposition.\n\nUnder `Open Items`, do not mark any exception `Closed`, do not state that the operations record is approved, and do not treat the missing confirmation or absent supporting files as resolved while the reviewer is unassigned and approval is pending.\n\nThroughout the brief, preserve the exact source figures, dates, reference identifiers, entity names, and statuses wherever they control the result, including break references, amounts, open dates, desk names, backup statuses, approval state, and supporting file statuses. Define abbreviations on first use, keep the tone conservative, and pair every exception with its controlling record and unresolved condition rather than asserting a conclusion.",
