    "full_prompt": "MATERIAL 1:\n[Continues under: § 240.10b-10 Confirmation of transactions.]\n\n(i) The date the transaction was executed, the identity of the single security or narrow-based security index underlying the contract for the security futures product, the number of contracts of such security futures product purchased or sold, the price, and the delivery month;\n\n(ii) The source and amount of any remuneration received or to be received by the broker or dealer in connection with the transaction, including, but not limited to, markups, commissions, costs, fees, and other charges incurred in connection with the transaction, provided, however, that if no remuneration is to be paid for an initiating transaction until the occurrence of the corresponding liquidating transaction, that the broker or dealer may disclose the amount of remuneration only on the confirmation for the liquidating transaction;\n\n(iii) The fact that information about the time of the execution of the transaction, the identity of the other party to the contract, and whether the broker or dealer is acting as agent for such customer, as agent for some other person, as agent for both such customer and some other person, or as principal for its own account, and if the broker or dealer is acting as principal, whether it is engaging in a block transaction or an exchange of security futures products for physical securities, will be available upon written request of the customer; and\n\n(iv) Whether payment for order flow is received by the broker or dealer for such transactions, the amount of this payment and the fact that the source and nature of the compensation received in connection with the particular transaction will be furnished upon written request of the customer; provided, however, that brokers or dealers that do not receive payment for order flow have no disclosure obligation under this paragraph.\n\nQUERY:\nPrepare a record retrieval readiness brief for the records evidence segment covering § 240.10b-10 confirmation of transactions for security futures products. Use only the supplied rule text; do not add external facts, customary recordkeeping practices, or assumptions about broker-dealer systems. Where the supplied text does not establish a retrieval element, label that element `Not Determinable`.\n\nStructure the brief with level-2 headings `Scope`, `Retrieval Elements`, `Readiness Findings`, and `Open Items` in that order. Under `Retrieval Elements`, provide a table that lists each disclosure element in the order it appears in the rule text, with columns for the rule paragraph, the exact operative phrase from the rule, the retrieval status, and the data field to be retrieved.\n\nReturn exactly four readiness findings, one for each disclosure element, ordered by the element's appearance in the rule text. Preserve the rule's exact terms wherever they control the retrieval requirement, including `single security or narrow-based security index`, `security futures product`, `payment for order flow`, and the phrase `upon written request of the customer`. Do not paraphrase or substitute equivalent terms.\n\nFor each finding, cite the exact rule paragraph and quote the operative phrase from the supplied text that creates the retrieval obligation. Treat the supplied text as the current rule text for § 240.10b-10, and state that no other material in the packet establishes whether any broker-dealer has adopted or implemented these requirements.\n\nApply the following conditional trigger to each element: if the rule text states that a broker-dealer has no disclosure obligation under a paragraph, mark that element's retrieval readiness as `Not Required`; otherwise mark it as `Retrieval Required` and identify the data field to be retrieved. Cover each of the four disclosure elements as a distinct retrieval topic: execution date and security futures product identification, remuneration source and amount, written-request availability facts, and payment for order flow disclosure.\n\nUnder `Open Items`, list any retrieval element whose status cannot be established from the supplied text as `Not Determinable`, and identify what additional evidence would be needed to resolve each open item.",
