    "work_product": "group payment notices and order-flow definition confirmation conditional disclosure analysis brief",
    "full_prompt": "MATERIAL 1:\n[Continues under: § 240.10b-10 Confirmation of transactions.]\n\n(C) To advise each customer in the group if a payment is not received from the designated person on behalf of the group within 10 days of a date certain specified in the arrangement for delivery of that payment by the designated person and thereafter to send to each such customer the written notification described in paragraph (a) of this section for the next three succeeding payments.\n\n(7) NMS stock shall have the meaning provided in § 242.600 of this chapter.\n\n(8) Payment for order flow shall mean any monetary payment, service, property, or other benefit that results in remuneration, compensation, or consideration to a broker or dealer from any broker or dealer, national securities exchange, registered securities association, or exchange member in return for the routing of customer orders by such broker or dealer to any broker or dealer, national securities exchange, registered securities association, or exchange member for execution, including but not limited to: research, clearance, custody, products or services; reciprocal agreements for the provision of order flow; adjustment of a broker or dealer's unfavorable trading errors; offers to participate as underwriter in public offerings; stock loans or shared interest accrued thereon; discounts, rebates, or any other reductions of or credits against any fee to, or expense or other financial obligation of, the broker or dealer routing a customer order that exceeds that fee, expense or financial obligation.\n\nQUERY:\nPrepare a confirmation conditional disclosure analysis brief under § 240.10b-10 of the eCFR rule text supplied. The brief must address four distinct analytical topics in the following order, each in its own numbered section: (1) group payment notice obligation, (2) payment for order flow definition, (3) 10-day deadline condition, and (4) disclosure classification.\n\nFor the group payment notice obligation topic, identify the condition under which a broker or dealer must advise each customer in the group, using the exact statutory terms 'payment for order flow', 'NMS stock', '10 days of a date certain', and 'next three succeeding payments' wherever they control the analysis. Do not substitute or paraphrase these terms.\n\nFor the payment for order flow definition topic, classify each enumerated example of remuneration in the statutory definition as either `Included` or `Excluded` based solely on whether it falls within the statutory language of 'monetary payment, service, property, or other benefit' received in return for routing customer orders. Use only the exact labels `Disclosure Required`, `No Disclosure Required`, and `Not Determinable` when stating the conditional disclosure classification for each analytical topic.\n\nFor the 10-day deadline condition topic, state that the applicable time window is 10 days from the date certain specified in the arrangement, and determine whether a payment received after that window triggers the obligation to advise each customer in the group. If the arrangement does not specify a date certain for delivery of the group payment, assign `Not Determinable` to the 10-day deadline condition and state that the disclosure obligation under the group payment notice provision cannot be triggered without that date.\n\nIdentify the supplied text as rule text from § 240.10b-10 and state that it is the current governing standard for the analysis, not staff guidance or a proposal. The brief must apply the group payment notice and payment for order flow provisions to determine the conditional disclosure obligations under § 240.10b-10.",
