    "full_prompt": "MATERIAL 1:\n[Continues under: § 240.10b-10 Confirmation of transactions.]\n\n(2) Transitional provision. (i) Broker-dealers are not required to comply with paragraph (e)(1)(iii) of this section until June 1, 2003, Provided that, if, not withstanding the absence of the disclosure required in that paragraph, the broker-dealer receives a written request from a customer for the information described in paragraph (e)(1)(iii) of this section, the broker-dealer must make the information available to the customer; and\n\n(ii) Broker-dealers are not required to comply with paragraph (e)(1)(iv) of this section until June 1, 2003.\n\n(f) The Commission may exempt any broker or dealer from the requirements of paragraphs (a) and (b) of this section with regard to specific transactions of specific classes of transactions for which the broker or dealer will provide alternative procedures to effect the purposes of this section; any such exemption may be granted subject to compliance with such alternative procedures and upon such other stated terms and conditions as the Commission may impose.\n\nQUERY:\nPrepare a transitional confirmation provisions and exemptions confirmation conditional disclosure analysis brief using only the supplied text of § 240.10b-10. Structure the brief with four level-2 sections in this order: 'Transitional Provision', 'Conditional Disclosure Trigger', 'Exemption Authority', and 'Open Conditions'.\n\nIn the 'Transitional Provision' section, state that the supplied material is rule text under § 240.10b-10, and present the transitional provision as a current regulatory requirement rather than staff guidance or a proposal. For each analytical component in this section, identify the exact provision of § 240.10b-10 relied upon, including the paragraph reference and the specific clause that supplies the requirement or condition. Preserve the exact rule references and dates, including 'June 1, 2003', 'paragraph (e)(1)(iii)', 'paragraph (e)(1)(iv)', and 'paragraphs (a) and (b)', wherever they control the analysis. Determine the current applicability of the transitional provision by testing whether the relevant date is before June 1, 2003, and state the timing status for each of paragraphs (e)(1)(iii) and (e)(1)(iv) separately.\n\nIn the 'Conditional Disclosure Trigger' section, apply the following conditional rule: if a broker-dealer receives a written request from a customer for the information described in paragraph (e)(1)(iii), the broker-dealer must make the information available to the customer; otherwise, the transitional non-compliance period continues until June 1, 2003. Map this trigger to the exact clause in the transitional provision that supplies it.\n\nIn the 'Exemption Authority' section, identify the Commission as the sole authority that may grant an exemption from paragraphs (a) and (b) of this section with regard to specific transactions or specific classes of transactions. State that no exemption exists unless the Commission has granted one subject to compliance with alternative procedures and upon such other stated terms and conditions as the Commission may impose. Identify the exact provision that supplies this authority.\n\nIn the 'Open Conditions' section, label any conclusion that cannot be established from the supplied rule text as 'Not Determinable', without adding outside facts about broker-dealer practices or Commission actions. Close the brief with a one-sentence 'Next action:' line stating what must be established before a broker-dealer can rely on the transitional non-compliance period or an exemption.",
