    "full_prompt": "MATERIAL 1:\n§ 240.17a-4 Records to be preserved by certain exchange members, brokers and dealers.\n\nThis section applies to the following types of entities: A member of a national securities exchange who transacts a business in securities directly with others than members of a national securities exchange; a broker or dealer who transacts a business in securities through the medium of a member of a national securities exchange; a broker or dealer, including an OTC derivatives dealer as that term is defined in § 240.3b-12, registered pursuant to section 15 of the Act (15 U.S.C. 78 o ); a security-based swap dealer registered pursuant to section 15F of the Act (15 U.S.C. 78 o -10) that is also a broker or dealer, including an OTC derivatives dealer, registered pursuant to section 15 of the Act; and a major security-based swap participant registered pursuant to section 15F of the Act that is also a broker or dealer, including an OTC derivatives dealer, registered pursuant to section 15 of the Act. Section 240.18a-6 (rather than this section) applies to the following types of entities: A security-based swap dealer registered pursuant to section 15F of the Act that is not also a broker or dealer, including an OTC derivatives dealer, registered pursuant to section 15 of the Act; and a major security-based swap participant registered pursuant to section 15F of the Act that is not also a broker or dealer, including an OTC derivatives dealer, registered pursuant to section 15 of the Act.\n\nMATERIAL 2:\n§ 240.17a-3 Records to be made by certain exchange members, brokers and dealers.\n\nThis section applies to the following types of entities: A member of a national securities exchange who transacts a business in securities directly with others than members of a national securities exchange; a broker or dealer who transacts a business in securities through the medium of a member of a national securities exchange; a broker or dealer, including an OTC derivatives dealer as that term is defined in § 240.3b-12, registered pursuant to section 15 of the Act (15 U.S.C. 78 o ); a security-based swap dealer registered pursuant to section 15F of the Act (15 U.S.C. 78 o -10) that is also a broker or dealer, including an OTC derivatives dealer, registered pursuant to section 15 of the Act; and a major security-based swap participant registered pursuant to section 15F of the Act that is also a broker or dealer, including an OTC derivatives dealer, registered pursuant to section 15 of the Act. Section 240.18a-5 (rather than this section) applies to the following types of entities: A security-based swap dealer registered pursuant to section 15F of the Act that is not also a broker or dealer, including an OTC derivatives dealer, registered pursuant to section 15 of the Act; and a major security-based swap participant registered pursuant to section 15F of the Act that is not also a broker or dealer, including an OTC derivatives dealer, registered pursuant to section 15 of the Act.\n\nQUERY:\nProduce a record retention applicability recordkeeping implementation evidence specification brief using only the supplied text of § 240.17a-3 (Records to be made) and § 240.17a-4 (Records to be preserved). The brief must contain four level-2 headings in this order: `Scope and Applicability`, `Cross-Provision Comparison`, `Classification of Entity Types`, and `Implementation Evidence Specification`, with a short `Open Items` paragraph immediately after the classification table.\n\nBegin the brief with a one-sentence statement identifying the two governing provisions and the cross-reference pair that divides their applicability, and close with a `Next action:` line tied to the highest-priority unresolved classification or evidence gap.\n\nCover the following topics: the applicability list in § 240.17a-3, the applicability list in § 240.17a-4, the cross-references to § 240.18a-5 and § 240.18a-6, the entity-type classification results, and the implementation evidence specification for each classification.\n\nFor each entity type listed in the two provisions, classify it into exactly one of `Subject to § 240.17a-3`, `Subject to § 240.17a-4`, `Subject to Both`, or `Subject to Neither` based solely on the applicability language in the two supplied texts. Use only those exact labels in the classification status field. If an entity type is described as subject to § 240.18a-5 or § 240.18a-6 in the supplied text, assign the classification `Subject to Neither` for the corresponding record-making or record-preservation provision and identify the cross-referenced provision that applies instead. Label any entity type whose treatment cannot be established from the supplied provisions as `Not Determinable`.\n\nFor every classification and cross-provision comparison, identify the supporting provision by its exact section number and quote the specific applicability language relied upon, keeping the source label adjacent to each entity-type row and each cross-reference finding. Preserve the exact section numbers, statutory citations, and entity-type descriptions from the supplied texts wherever they control a classification or cross-reference finding, without paraphrasing or relabeling them.\n\nIdentify both supplied texts as rule text and distinguish the current applicability provisions from the cross-referenced provisions in § 240.18a-5 and § 240.18a-6, which are cited but not supplied and therefore cannot be treated as establishing record-making or record-preservation requirements in this brief.",
