    "full_prompt": "MATERIAL 1:\n[Continues under: § 240.17a-4 Records to be preserved by certain exchange members, brokers and dealers.]\n\n(v)(A) Have at all times filed with the designated examining authority for the member, broker, or dealer the following undertakings with respect to such records signed by either a designated executive officer or designated third party (hereinafter, the “undersigned”):\n\nThe undersigned hereby undertakes to furnish promptly to the U.S. Securities and Exchange Commission (“Commission”), its designees or representatives, any self- regulatory organization of which [Name of the Member, Broker, or Dealer] is a member, or any State securities regulator having jurisdiction over [Name of the Member, Broker, or Dealer], upon reasonable request, such information as is deemed necessary by the staff of the Commission, any self-regulatory organization of which [Name of the Member, Broker, or Dealer] is a member, or any State securities regulator having jurisdiction over [Name of the Member, Broker, or Dealer], and to download copies of a record and its audit trail (if applicable) preserved by means of an electronic recordkeeping system of [Name of the Member, Broker, or Dealer] into both a human readable format and a reasonably usable electronic format in the event of a failure on the part of [Name of the Member, Broker, or Dealer] to download a requested record or its audit trail (if applicable). Furthermore, the undersigned hereby undertakes to take reasonable steps to provide access to the information preserved by means of an electronic recordkeeping system of [Name of the Member, Broker, or Dealer], including, as appropriate, downloading any record required to be maintained and preserved by [Name of the Member, Broker, or Dealer] pursuant to §§ 240.17a-3 and 240.17a-4 in a format acceptable to the staff of the Commission, any self-regulatory organization of which [Name of the Member, Broker, or Dealer] is a member, or any State securities regulator having jurisdiction over [Name of the Member, Broker, or Dealer]. Specifically, the undersigned will take reasonable steps to, in the event of a failure on the part of [Name of the Member, Broker, or Dealer] to download the record into a human readable format or a reasonably usable electronic format and after reasonable notice to [Name of the Member, Broker, or Dealer], download the record into a human readable format or a reasonably usable electronic format at the request of the staffs of the Commission, any self-regulatory organization of which [Name of the Member, Broker, or Dealer] is a member, or any State securities regulator having jurisdiction over [Name of the Member, Broker, or Dealer].\n\nMATERIAL 2:\n[Continues under: § 240.17a-3 Records to be made by certain exchange members, brokers and dealers.]\n\n(9) A record with respect to each cash, margin, and security-based swap account with such member, broker or dealer indicating, as applicable:\n\n(i) The name and address of the beneficial owner of such account;\n\n(ii) Except with respect to exempt employee benefit plan securities as defined in § 240.14a-1(d), but only to the extent such securities are held by employee benefit plans established by the issuer of the securities, whether or not the beneficial owner of securities registered in the name of such members, brokers or dealers, or a registered clearing agency or its nominee objects to disclosure of his or her identity, address, and securities positions to issuers;\n\n(iii) In the case of a margin account, the signature of such owner; provided that, in the case of a joint account or an account of a corporation, such records are required only in respect of the person or persons authorized to transact business for such account; and\n\n(iv) For each security-based swap account, a record of the unique identification code of such counterparty, the name and address of such counterparty, and a record of the authorization of each person the counterparty has granted authority to transact business in the security-based swap account.\n\nQUERY:\nPrepare a record access undertakings recordkeeping implementation evidence specification brief that integrates the record-content requirements of § 240.17a-3(9) with the access and download undertakings of § 240.17a-4(v)(A). Structure the brief in exactly four numbered sections, in this order: (1) record-content requirements, (2) access and download undertakings, (3) failure-triggered obligations, and (4) implementation evidence specification.\n\nSection 1 must identify, for each cash, margin, and security-based swap account, the record elements required by § 240.17a-3(9): the name and address of the beneficial owner; the disclosure objection status, including the exemption for exempt employee benefit plan securities as defined in § 240.14a-1(d) only to the extent such securities are held by employee benefit plans established by the issuer; the signature requirement for margin accounts, limited in joint or corporate accounts to persons authorized to transact business; and, for each security-based swap account, the unique identification code, name and address of the counterparty, and the authorization record for each person granted authority to transact business.\n\nSection 2 must identify the undertakings required by § 240.17a-4(v)(A) to be filed at all times with the designated examining authority, signed by a designated executive officer or designated third party: the undertaking to furnish promptly, upon reasonable request, information deemed necessary by the staff of the Commission, any self-regulatory organization of which the member, broker, or dealer is a member, or any State securities regulator having jurisdiction; the undertaking to download copies of a record and its audit trail, if applicable, into both human readable and reasonably usable electronic format; and the undertaking to take reasonable steps to provide access to information preserved by the electronic recordkeeping system, including downloading any record required to be maintained and preserved under §§ 240.17a-3 and 240.17a-4 in a format acceptable to those recipients.\n\nSection 3 must state the conditional trigger: if the member, broker, or dealer fails to download a requested record or its audit trail, the undersigned must, after reasonable notice to the member, broker, or dealer, download the record into human readable and reasonably usable electronic format at the request of the staff of the Commission, any self-regulatory organization of which the member, broker, or dealer is a member, or any State securities regulator having jurisdiction.\n\nSection 4 must specify the implementation evidence to be collected and retained, including the signed undertakings filed with the designated examining authority and the account records required by § 240.17a-3(9), and identify any missing signature, filing, or account record needed to close the file. For each requirement, cite the exact subsection and language from § 240.17a-3(9) or § 240.17a-4(v)(A) that supports it. Identify the control responsibilities of the designated executive officer or designated third party signatory and of the Commission, self-regulatory organizations, and State securities regulators in maintaining and exercising access. State which signature and filing evidence under § 240.17a-4(v)(A) and which account-record authorization evidence under § 240.17a-3(9) are required before the undertakings can be treated as effective, and preserve any missing signature or filing as an open condition. Treat both §§ 240.17a-3 and 240.17a-4 as current rule text imposing obligations, not as staff guidance or a non-binding proposal.\n\nBegin the brief with a one-sentence statement of the implementation evidence status. End with a one-sentence readiness gate identifying any evidence still required before the record access undertakings can be considered fully implemented.",
