    "workflow": "Execution, Monitoring, Reporting, and Operations",
    "task": "Recordkeeping implementation evidence specification and cross-provision requirements analysis",
    "work_product": "delegation and micrographic copies recordkeeping implementation evidence specification brief — evidence-integrated revision",
    "full_prompt": "MATERIAL 1:\n[Continues under: § 240.17a-4 Records to be preserved by certain exchange members, brokers and dealers.]\n\n( 1 ) Appoint in writing up to two designated officers who will take the steps necessary to fulfill the obligations of the designated executive officer set forth in the undertakings in the event the designated executive officer is unable to fulfill those obligations; and\n\n( 2 ) Appoint in writing up to three designated specialists.\n\n(C) The appointment of, or reliance on, a designated officer or designated specialist does not relieve the designated executive officer of the obligations set forth in the undertaking.\n\n(4) A broker-dealer using a micrographic media system must:\n\n(i) At all times have available, for examination by the staffs of the Commission, self-regulatory organizations of which it is a member, and any State securities regulator having jurisdiction over the member, broker, or dealer, facilities for immediate, easily readable projection or production of micrographic media and for producing easily readable images;\n\n(ii) Be ready at all times to provide, and immediately provide, any facsimile enlargement which the staffs of the Commission, any self-regulatory organization of which it is a member, or any State securities regulator having jurisdiction over the member, broker, or dealer may request;\n\n(iii) Store, separately from the original, a duplicate copy of the record stored on any medium acceptable under this section for the time required; and\n\n(iv) Organize and index accurately all information maintained on both original and duplicate storage media.\n\nMATERIAL 2:\n[Continues under: § 240.17a-3 Records to be made by certain exchange members, brokers and dealers.]\n\n(7)(i) A memorandum of each purchase or sale of a security, other than for the purchase or sale of a security-based swap, for the account of the member, broker or dealer showing the price and, to the extent feasible, the time of execution; and, in addition, where the purchase or sale is with a customer other than a broker or dealer, a memorandum of each order received, showing the time of receipt; the terms and conditions of the order and of any modification thereof; the account for which it was entered; the identity of each associated person, if any, responsible for the account; the identity of any other person who entered or accepted the order on behalf of the customer, or, if a customer entered the order on an electronic system, a notation of that entry. The memorandum need not show the identity of any person other than the associated person responsible for the account who may have entered the order if the order is entered into an electronic system that generates the memorandum and if that system is not capable of receiving an entry of the identity of any person other than the responsible associated person. In the circumstance in the preceding sentence, the member, broker or dealer must produce upon request by a representative of a securities regulatory authority a separate record that identifies each other person. An order with a customer other than a member, broker or dealer entered pursuant to the exercise of discretionary authority by the member, broker or dealer, or associated person thereof, must be so designated.\n\nQUERY:\nPrepare a delegation and micrographic copies recordkeeping implementation evidence specification brief for a broker-dealer's compliance implementation reviewer. Begin with a one-sentence readiness statement indicating whether the recordkeeping implementation evidence specification is complete or which evidence remains outstanding, then present exactly four numbered evidence specification sections ordered from the most foundational preservation and delegation requirement to the most conditional electronic-entry exception. Write for a compliance implementation reviewer: in each section, separate the governing provision, the evidence required to demonstrate implementation, the responsible party, and the resulting status or gap. State that both § 240.17a-3 and § 240.17a-4 are current rule text, not staff guidance or proposal, and treat every obligation they contain as a current requirement rather than an illustrative example. Preserve the exact terms, counts, and conditional language from both provisions, including 'up to two designated officers,' 'up to three designated specialists,' 'separately from the original,' 'for the time required,' and the electronic-system capability condition, without paraphrasing or altering their controlling effect.\n\nFor each recordkeeping obligation, connect the active evidence required, the governing provision from § 240.17a-3 or § 240.17a-4, and the resulting implementation action in a single traceable chain, without presenting facts, provisions, and actions as disconnected fragments. For each recordkeeping requirement, list the specific records or documentation that must be created, maintained, or produced as implementation evidence, including the written officer and specialist appointments, the separately stored duplicate copy, and the separate record identifying each other person under the electronic-entry exception.\n\nCover the governance and control responsibilities in the brief, including the written appointment of up to two designated officers and up to three designated specialists, the non-relief of the designated executive officer, the availability and readiness obligations for micrographic media, and the separate-record production duty for the electronic-entry exception. Identify the approval or authorization evidence required for the delegation structure, including the written appointments of designated officers and specialists, and state that the designated executive officer remains responsible despite any appointment or reliance.\n\nFor the duplicate-copy storage requirement in § 240.17a-4, specify the time period during which the duplicate copy must be stored separately from the original and state the applicable storage window with its source language preserved. Apply the electronic-entry exception conditionally: if an order is entered into an electronic system that generates the memorandum and that system is not capable of receiving the identity of any person other than the responsible associated person, then the memorandum need not show that other person's identity, but the separate record identifying each other person must be produced upon request by a securities regulatory authority representative.\n\nClose with a 'Next action:' line tied to the highest-priority unresolved evidence gap identified in the brief.",
