    "full_prompt": "MATERIAL 1:\n[Continues under: § 240.17a-4 Records to be preserved by certain exchange members, brokers and dealers.]\n\n(i)(1)(i) If the records required to be maintained and preserved pursuant to the provisions of § 240.17a-3 and this section are prepared or maintained by an outside service bureau, depository, bank, or other recordkeeping service, including a recordkeeping service that owns and operates the servers or other storage devices on which the records are preserved or maintained, (none of which operate pursuant to § 240.17a-3(c)) on behalf of the member, broker, or dealer required to maintain and preserve such records, such outside entity must file with the Commission a written undertaking in a form acceptable to the Commission, signed by a duly authorized person, to the effect that such records are the property of the member, broker, or dealer required to maintain and preserve such records and will be surrendered promptly on request of the member, broker, or dealer and including the following provision:\n\nWith respect to any books and records maintained or preserved on behalf of [Name of the Member, Broker, or Dealer], the undersigned hereby undertakes to permit examination of such books and records at any time or from time to time during business hours by representatives or designees of the Securities and Exchange Commission and to promptly furnish to said Commission or its designee true, correct, complete and current hard copies of any or all or any part of such books and records.\n\nMATERIAL 2:\n[Continues under: § 240.17a-4 Records to be preserved by certain exchange members, brokers and dealers.]\n\n(xiii) Detail relating to information for possession or control requirements under § 240.15c3-3 or § 240.18a-4, as applicable and reported in Part II or IIA of Form X-17A-5 (§ 249.617 of this chapter), as applicable;\n\n(xiv) Detail relating to information for security-based swap possession or control requirements under § 240.15c3-3 or § 240.18a-4, as applicable, and reported in Part II or IIA of Form X-17A-5 (§ 249.617 of this chapter);\n\n(xv) Detail of all items, not otherwise substantiated, which are charged or credited in the Computation of Net Capital pursuant to § 240.15c3-1 or § 240.18a-1, as applicable, such as cash margin deficiencies, deductions related to securities values and undue concentration, aged securities differences, and insurance claims receivable;\n\n(xvi) Detail relating to the calculation of the risk margin amount pursuant to § 240.15c3-1(c)(17) or § 240.18a-1(c)(6), as applicable; and\n\n(xvii) Other schedules which are specifically prescribed by the Commission as necessary to support information reported as required by §§ 240.17a-5, 240.17a-12, and 240.18a-7, as applicable.\n\nMATERIAL 3:\n[Continues under: § 240.17a-3 Records to be made by certain exchange members, brokers and dealers.]\n\n(5) The broker or dealer upon request furnishes promptly to representatives of the Commission the records required by paragraphs (a)(1), (3), and (5) of this section as well as the records required by 17 CFR 23.201, 23.202, 23.402, and 23.501 as they pertain to security-based swap and swap transactions and positions in the format applicable to that category of record as set forth in this section; and\n\n(6) The broker or dealer provides notice of its intent to utilize this paragraph (b) by notifying in writing the Commission, both at the principal office of the Commission in Washington, DC, and at the regional office of the Commission for the region in which the registrant has its principal place of business, as well as by notifying in writing the registrant's designated examining authority.\n\n(c) A member of a national securities exchange, or a broker or dealer registered pursuant to section 15 of the Act (15 U.S.C. 78 o ), that introduces accounts on a fully-disclosed basis, is not required to make or keep such records of transactions cleared for such member, broker or dealer as are made and kept by a clearing broker or dealer pursuant to the requirements of this section and § 240.17a-4. Nothing in this paragraph (c) will be deemed to relieve such member, broker or dealer from the responsibility that such books and records be accurately maintained and preserved as specified in this section and § 240.17a-4.\n\nQUERY:\nProduce an outside recordkeeping services recordkeeping implementation evidence specification brief — evidence-integrated revision. Begin with a one-sentence implementation-readiness conclusion stating whether the evidence specification is ready for use or what prevents readiness. Use only the supplied materials and label any result that cannot be established from them as `Not Determinable`.\n\nOrganize the brief under level-2 headings `Undertaking`, `Record Schedules`, and `Furnishing and Notice`, in that order, followed by a short `Readiness Gate` paragraph. Cover the undertaking provision, the record detail schedules, and the furnishing and notice provisions as distinct topics. Return exactly three evidence-specification entries, one per covered topic, ordered by implementation dependency from the undertaking through the record schedules to the furnishing and notice provisions.\n\nFor the `Undertaking` topic, use § 240.17a-4(i)(1)(i) to specify the written undertaking that an outside service bureau, depository, bank, or other recordkeeping service must file with the Commission when it prepares or maintains records required under § 240.17a-3 and § 240.17a-4 on behalf of a member, broker, or dealer. Identify the duly authorized person who must sign the undertaking and state which signatory evidence controls acceptance of the filing. List the records to retain in the implementation workpaper and identify any missing document needed to close the file. Identify the Commission filing triggered by the undertaking provision and state the recipient and any source-supported deadline or timing condition.\n\nFor the `Record Schedules` topic, use § 240.17a-4(b)(xiii) through (xvii) to specify the detail records relating to possession or control requirements, security-based swap possession or control requirements, unsubstantiated items charged or credited in the Computation of Net Capital, the risk margin amount calculation, and other Commission-prescribed schedules. Separate the design of the implementation control from the evidence that the control operated, and identify the control owner for each evidence gap. List the records to retain in the implementation workpaper and identify any missing document needed to close the file.\n\nFor the `Furnishing and Notice` topic, use § 240.17a-3(b)(5) and (6) and § 240.17a-3(c) to specify the broker's or dealer's obligation to furnish records promptly to Commission representatives upon request and to provide written notice of intent to utilize paragraph (b) to the Commission at its Washington, DC, principal office, the relevant regional office, and the designated examining authority. Address the fully-disclosed account exception in § 240.17a-3(c) and state that it does not relieve the introducing member, broker, or dealer from responsibility for accurate maintenance and preservation. Identify the Commission as the recipient of the notice and state which recipient evidence controls acceptance of the filing. Separate the design of the implementation control from the evidence that the control operated, and identify the control owner for each evidence gap. List the records to retain in the implementation workpaper and identify any missing document needed to close the file.\n\nFor each entry, label the specification `Complete` only if every element of the applicable provision is supported by an identified record; otherwise label it `Open` and list the missing element. Identify each cited provision as current rule text and do not present it as staff guidance, a proposal, or a non-binding example. Close with a one-sentence next-action line tied to the highest-priority missing evidence.",
